WEBVTT

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:24.650
15 years ago, Northern Atlantic Ocean

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:42.530
Kaidou Wataru (41)

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:43.020
Iceberg, 12 o'clock!

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.390
Hard to port!

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:08.920
Captain ...

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:10.630
Captain, are you all right?!

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:12.980
Excuse me.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.230
Captain ...

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:17.940
Captain!

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:19.800
Please hold on, Captain!

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:35.480
First-mate ...

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:17.150
Half a month ago, Nishitama City

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:21.200
Yashiro

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:47.640
Yashiro Hideto (49)

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:22.100
It's so beautiful.

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:27.270
I wish I could show Shinichi this beautiful sunset.

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:32.690
I see it.

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:36.740
Wha... What?!

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:38.610
You'll be able to see better from up here.

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:43.960
It's true that I can see better now,

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:45.980
but what an embarrassing position ...

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:49.800
We saw that, Conan!

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:51.350
Crap!

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:53.420
Let me down, Ran-neechan!

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:55.090
We saw you, we saw you!

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:58.520
We saw you! You were indulging
with Ran-san again, weren't you?

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:00.550
Idiot, it's nothing like that!

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:02.950
Your face is red, Conan-kun.

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:05.470
What are you talking about?
That's just because of the sunset.

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:09.260
He's turning red!

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:11.430
Stupid! No, I'm not!

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:14.520
What are you talking about?

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:17.520
I'm telling you, it's because of the sunset!

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:21.030
It's the same as that time.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:22.400
Eh? What is?

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:25.800
It's nothing.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:27.860
What is it? Tell me!

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:29.830
I'm telling you, it's nothing!

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:25.090
Detective CONAN

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:25.090
Strategy Above The Depths

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.310
I'm high school detective Kudou Shinichi.

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:36.280
Original story: Aoyama Gosho

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:36.580
While I went to an amusement park
with my childhood friend Mouri Ran ...

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:40.500
I witnessed a suspicious transaction by a man in black.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:41.070
Script: Furuuichi Issei

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:43.050
Because my attention was focused on the transaction,

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:46.110
I didn't notice another member
approaching me from behind.

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:51.200
Music: Oono Katsuo

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:50.640
He forced me to take some poison.

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:52.540
And when I came to ...

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:55.410
My body had shrunk!

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:59.210
Character Design: Sudou Masatomo

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:58.290
If the men in black find out that Kudou Shinichi is still alive,

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:01.670
they'll come after me again and endanger the lives of my friends and family.

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:04.130
Art Director: Shibuya Yukihiro

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:05.950
Following Professor Agasa's advice,
I decided to hide my identity.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:08.920
Director of Photography: Nomura Takashi

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:09.340
When Ran asked my name,
I suddenly blurted out, "Edogawa Conan."

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:14.570
In order to get information about the men in black,
I moved in with Ran and her father, a detective.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:21.620
I'm from Teitan Elementary Grade 1,
Class B. Kojima Genta.

00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:24.450
The same, Tsuburaya Mitsuhiko.

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:26.340
Yoshida Ayumi.

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:27.760
Along with my apprentice, Conan ...

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:28.900
And Ai-chan ...

00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:35.050
We are the Detective Boys!

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:39.860
These sparkling detective badges on our chests
each contain a microscopic transceiver.

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:42.510
They also have homing signals.
It's the very latest technology!

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:49.870
These wristwatch flashlights are waterproof,
so you can even use them in the ocean!

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:54.100
Edogawa Conan: Takayama Minami

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:54.260
These two devices are Professor Agasa's inventions.

00:06:55.870 --> 00:07:00.520
The Professor's made other unique
gadgets for the shrunken me.

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:05.150
Most importantly, the Super Bowtie Voice Changer and the Wrist Watch Tranquilizer.

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:05.150
Wrist Watch Tranquilizer

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:05.150
Super Bowtie Voice Changer

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:09.640
Mouri Kogorou: Kamiya Akira

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:10.990
Thanks to these two devices, the famous detective "Sleeping Kogorou" was born.

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:20.120
You know, Haibara-san's a bit cool.
Or rather mature for her age.

00:07:14.230 --> 00:07:18.110
Haibara Ai: Hayashibara Megumi

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:22.420
Kudou Shinichi: Yamaguchi Kappei

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:22.420
Of course she is.

00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:26.250
Haibara Ai's real name is Miyano Shiho.

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:30.080
She was originally a part of the Black Syndicate.

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:36.240
But to get away from the organization, she took the same drug that I'd been forced to take, and her body shrank as well.

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:43.290
And so I, who went from being a high school
detective to an elementary school detective,

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:46.730
have been solving one complex case after another,

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:51.400
As I secretly try to find out
the identities of the men in black.

00:07:52.310 --> 00:07:53.910
But Uncle ...

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:58.320
Producers:

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:58.320
Suwa Michiko

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:57.490
If only his deductions would get a little better ...

00:08:00.110 --> 00:08:02.060
Even though I'm much smaller,
my intellect remains the same.

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:05.040
The detective with no unsolvable mysteries.

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:09.490
Director: Yamamoto Taiichiro

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:08.280
There's always only one truth!

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:25.440
Wow, it's so big!

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:27.230
It sure is luxurious.

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:28.750
Of course, it is.

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:32.110
Yashiro Group is a pretty big financial group.

00:08:32.670 --> 00:08:37.670
This is that 100-million dollar
group's first cruise ship ever built.

00:08:37.670 --> 00:08:39.490
It's gotta be this luxurious.

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:42.790
Welcome.

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:45.090
You must be Mouri-sama.

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:45.920
Uh, yes.

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:50.560
We're preparing your seats right now.
Please wait a moment.

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:55.550
Hey Professor. What is that?

00:08:56.360 --> 00:09:00.430
This? It's just a regular IC recorder.

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:05.020
I was thinking I could use it to immediately record my thoughts when I get hints or ideas for new inventions.

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:07.790
Oh, speaking of new inventions,

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:11.320
Tada! Cufflink speakers.

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:12.690
It contains a transceiver as well.

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:15.770
That's pretty cool.

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:17.660
These are awesome.

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:19.780
Those are some nice cuff links.

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:22.370
This is great. I'll borrow these for awhile.

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:23.640
But those are ...

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:28.790
You idiot. These things are made for dandy men like me.

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:32.040
It's still a bit too early for a kid like you.

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:33.800
But, Dad! Those are ...

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:36.820
It's fine, Ran-neechan.

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:39.610
I probably won't need them inside this ship anyways.

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:40.810
Mouri-san?

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:45.060
You're the famous detective,
Mouri Kogorou-san, right?

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:46.780
Yes, that's right ...

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:48.160
Cool!

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:49.560
What's with this guy?

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:53.450
I'm a script writer, Kusaka Hironari.

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:54.970
Kusaka Hironari (26)

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:55.360
I'm a big fan of yours, Mouri-san.

00:09:55.750 --> 00:09:57.340
Oh, thank you.

00:09:58.350 --> 00:09:59.740
Ah, this is ...

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:01.830
Akiyoshi Minako-san.

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:05.300
She's a sub-leader of the design team for this ship,

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:09.140
And she gave this ship, the St. Aphrodite, its beautiful name.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:10.790
Akiyoshi Minako (32)

00:10:09.140 --> 00:10:11.250
I'm Akiyoshi. Nice to meet you.

00:10:11.570 --> 00:10:13.750
I'm Mouri ...

00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:16.510
Wow, she's beautiful.

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:17.470
Yeah ...

00:10:18.190 --> 00:10:19.520
Excuse me, Mouri-sama.

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:23.800
Sorry to keep you waiting.
Your seats have been prepared.

00:10:23.800 --> 00:10:25.060
Oh, sorry.

00:10:25.460 --> 00:10:26.930
Could you add two more?

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:28.390
It's okay with you, right, Mouri-san?

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:29.970
Yeah ...

00:10:29.970 --> 00:10:31.290
Then, right this way.

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:37.900
Hey, isn't your dad acting a bit strange?

00:10:38.560 --> 00:10:39.390
Why?

00:10:39.390 --> 00:10:41.280
Well, because if it were the usual him, then ...

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:45.750
"Speaking of Aphrodite, she's the goddess of beauty and love!"

00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:49.960
"That name would be better suited
for you rather than for the ship."

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:54.130
That's what he would say, isn't it?

00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:59.340
That's probably because
Minako-san resembles my mother.

00:10:59.990 --> 00:11:01.840
I see.

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:04.350
Come to think of it, they do look alike.

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:09.010
That means she's the type Uncle
would have a hard time dealing with.

00:11:14.020 --> 00:11:19.400
I'm actually writing a drama series
set on a luxury cruise ship.

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:22.660
And I met Minako-san while I was collecting data.

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:23.750
More or less.

00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:24.950
I see ...

00:11:25.470 --> 00:11:29.090
By the way, Mouri-san.
You were invited of course, right?

00:11:29.550 --> 00:11:32.460
Or did they hire you to investigate some matters?

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:35.520
Well, how can I say this?
To say it was an invitation ...

00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:37.500
Actually, that's not it.

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:39.520
It's not?

00:11:39.520 --> 00:11:43.800
The ones invited were actually Sonoko's parents.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:47.280
Her father is the President of Suzuki Financial Group.

00:11:48.670 --> 00:11:53.580
But my parent just couldn't make it,
so I came in their place.

00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:56.730
And I thought, the more the merrier, so ...

00:11:57.130 --> 00:12:01.000
She managed to get invitations
for the eight of us as well.

00:12:02.270 --> 00:12:03.930
So that's how it was.

00:12:03.930 --> 00:12:06.780
Well, you could say that I'm just here as her guardian.

00:12:07.150 --> 00:12:08.570
Oh, I see.

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:11.290
I see ...

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:14.040
By the way, what kind of story are you writing?

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:18.020
Is it a story where someone goes
around the world on a luxury cruise?

00:12:18.020 --> 00:12:19.590
I like that.

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:20.550
Yeah!

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:26.050
Maybe it's a panic story like the Titanic
where the ship sinks in the middle of the ocean.

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:27.920
Hey, Ai-kun ...

00:12:29.710 --> 00:12:31.690
Speaking of sinking,

00:12:31.690 --> 00:12:37.740
There was a case a long time ago
where a Yashiro ship hit an iceberg.

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:40.820
Yes.  It was an accident during
the winter about 15 years ago.

00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:44.490
I believe that due to the misjudgment of the captain,

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:49.330
One staff member died, and the captain
ended his life along with the ship, too.

00:12:49.590 --> 00:12:50.900
Really?

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:53.030
What are we going to do if this ship sinks, too?

00:12:53.030 --> 00:12:55.370
I can only swim seven meters.

00:12:56.010 --> 00:12:57.430
Don't worry.

00:12:57.430 --> 00:12:59.920
The St. Aphrodite has a very good captain.

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:02.010
And there aren't any icebergs
around this part of the ocean.

00:13:02.530 --> 00:13:08.110
Although, if the ship sinks, the first ones to be
rescued will probably be those folks over there.

00:13:11.130 --> 00:13:14.980
Hey, isn't that Niemi-san, the former captain?

00:13:16.070 --> 00:13:19.260
And his company. Also, there's the very talented ...

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:21.650
Hey, that's Uruashi Shimai!

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:25.150
No matter how many times I see her, she's still got a nice body.

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:30.640
They were all personally invited by
the President of the Yashiro group.

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:33.910
The Yashiro family has arrived.

00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:38.920
Yashiro Takae (51)

00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:38.920
 Yashiro Entarou (78)

00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:38.920
His daughter Takae is married and is
the Chief Executive of Yashiro Cruiser.

00:13:39.570 --> 00:13:45.140
Oh, Chief Takae's husband died
in a car accident recently, right?

00:13:45.140 --> 00:13:46.360
Really?

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:48.640
Yes. Yashiro Hideto-sensei ...

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:53.280
He was my superior and the leader
of this ship's design crew.

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:55.160
I see.

00:13:55.160 --> 00:14:01.570
As I recall, he had a heart attack
while he was driving and drove off a cliff.

00:14:02.310 --> 00:14:04.070
Hey, it's the captain!

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:06.560
He's so cool!

00:14:08.830 --> 00:14:10.950
That's Captain Kaidou Wataru.

00:14:11.670 --> 00:14:14.510
Remember the accident 15 years ago
that we talked about earlier?

00:14:15.350 --> 00:14:18.740
He was the first-mate of that ship.

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:22.200
What? Something you don't find right?

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:24.800
About Yashiro Hideto-shi's accident?

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:31.180
The fact that his heart attack came while
he was in the middle of descending a hill ...

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:35.610
But according to the department's analysis,
there weren't any suspicious points, right?

00:14:35.610 --> 00:14:37.180
Yes, but ...

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:42.260
Why not? It's not a bad thing to
investigate until you're satisfied.

00:14:42.260 --> 00:14:45.230
I'll notify the department.

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:47.400
Thank you, sir.

00:14:48.090 --> 00:14:50.540
Satou-san, would you like me to help you?

00:14:50.540 --> 00:14:52.680
You still haven't finished your report though, right?

00:14:53.270 --> 00:14:53.780
Chiba-kun.

00:14:55.050 --> 00:14:56.180
Help me out a bit.

00:14:56.180 --> 00:14:57.250
R-right ...

00:15:07.470 --> 00:15:10.110
Now that the drinks are all set ...

00:15:10.110 --> 00:15:12.750
Wait. Let me do it, please?

00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:18.680
Well, then. To this fun cruise trip,

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:22.560
And to Ran's gold medal at the Kantou competition.

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:29.190
Cheers!

00:15:29.510 --> 00:15:30.860
Cheers!

00:15:32.890 --> 00:15:36.370
Thank you. Geez, Sonoko ...

00:15:36.770 --> 00:15:38.480
Hey, Ran-oneesan.

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:41.580
You're amazing, winning first place at the karate tournament.

00:15:41.810 --> 00:15:43.840
Kantou Taikai: Is a martial arts tournament, any form of martial arts is allowed, however, only hand to hand combat is allowed.

00:15:41.810 --> 00:15:43.840
Not only that, it was the Kantou competition.

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:46.340
That's awesome! Awesome, awesome!

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:50.860
So, did you get some kind of present from Kudou-kun?

00:15:50.860 --> 00:15:51.840
Shinichi?

00:15:53.210 --> 00:15:56.560
When I told him on the phone
all he said was, "Oh? Good for you".

00:15:56.870 --> 00:15:58.470
That's it?

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:02.060
He's probably all caught up
in his investigations on his cases.

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:03.480
That deduction maniac.

00:16:05.370 --> 00:16:08.850
That was right after I said
congratulations like mad as Conan ...

00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:15.320
I'm full!

00:16:15.920 --> 00:16:17.620
That was a good steak.

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:19.500
I wish I could eat it every day.

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:21.210
I wonder if dessert is next?

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:24.000
What's wrong?

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:26.760
I think I'm a bit seasick.

00:16:26.760 --> 00:16:29.520
Yeah, I'm also a little off ...

00:16:29.520 --> 00:16:31.540
You just drank too much alcohol.

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:33.800
Ran-chan, so strict ...

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:35.900
Geez ...

00:16:35.900 --> 00:16:37.480
You have a very interesting father.

00:16:37.480 --> 00:16:39.810
No, he's just a drunken old man.

00:16:40.260 --> 00:16:44.390
I'm sorry. I think I'll leave and rest in my room.

00:16:44.630 --> 00:16:46.010
Are you going to be okay?

00:16:46.010 --> 00:16:48.840
Yes. I have medicine in my room, so ...

00:16:48.840 --> 00:16:49.860
Take care ...

00:17:26.370 --> 00:17:30.120
Hey, Dad! Are you sure you're all right?

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:34.900
Mouri Kogorou is okay!

00:17:36.510 --> 00:17:38.320
It's fine, Ran-neechan.

00:17:38.810 --> 00:17:41.040
All that's left is to put him in bed, so ...

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:45.540
Sorry about this. Then, Conan-kun,
I'll leave Dad to you, okay?

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:46.250
Sure.

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:48.200
I'm sorry, Professor.

00:17:48.200 --> 00:17:49.970
It's not a problem.

00:17:49.970 --> 00:17:51.650
It's fine, it's fine.

00:17:53.060 --> 00:17:54.760
Good night, Ran-chan.

00:17:57.440 --> 00:17:58.640
It's open, Professor.

00:17:58.640 --> 00:17:59.650
Right.

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:03.640
All right. Us, too.

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:04.220
Yeah.

00:18:04.420 --> 00:18:06.070
Well then, Conan-kun.

00:18:06.070 --> 00:18:08.250
I'll leave Dad with you, okay?

00:18:14.790 --> 00:18:15.280
Eh?

00:18:15.590 --> 00:18:16.540
Yo!

00:18:16.540 --> 00:18:18.140
We're visiting!

00:18:18.140 --> 00:18:20.550
What are you guys doing all together?

00:18:20.550 --> 00:18:25.290
We've decided to give something to Ran-san
as a present for winning the competition.

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:26.290
What are these?

00:18:26.560 --> 00:18:30.290
They're pretty, huh? We picked them up on that island we visited this afternoon.

00:18:30.470 --> 00:18:33.760
We're going to make a gold medal from
these and give it to her as her present.

00:18:33.760 --> 00:18:37.710
It's a bit sad that she didn't get
anything from Shinichi-oniisan, right?

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:40.820
Good luck with that.

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:43.400
I'm going to take a bath.

00:18:43.400 --> 00:18:44.910
A bath?!

00:18:45.530 --> 00:18:47.520
What, you want to join me?

00:18:47.770 --> 00:18:49.340
No, that's ...

00:18:57.820 --> 00:19:00.530
I'll read your schedule for tomorrow.

00:19:00.990 --> 00:19:05.890
Your breakfast will be at 7:00 A.M., I will bring you a western-style meal set to your room.

00:19:03.490 --> 00:19:06.330
Tsujimoto Natsuho (25)

00:19:05.890 --> 00:19:09.590
After that, Chief Takae will be at a squash session with Madam Niemi at 9 A.M.

00:19:09.590 --> 00:19:12.260
We've booked a court on the 7th floor.

00:19:12.260 --> 00:19:15.340
The President will attend a gathering at 9:30 A.M.

00:19:15.470 --> 00:19:18.510
It has been moved to the pool bar on the 3rd floor.

00:19:19.000 --> 00:19:23.760
After the squash game, Chief Takae will return to the room around 9:30 A.M.

00:19:44.670 --> 00:19:46.280
It feels so good!

00:19:46.690 --> 00:19:51.320
Indeed, morning tea is really
something in the salty breeze.

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:56.090
It's really something.

00:19:56.620 --> 00:19:59.050
Yeah, it really is something.

00:19:59.320 --> 00:20:01.220
It really is something.

00:20:11.410 --> 00:20:14.220
Hey, did you see Chief Takae's legs?

00:20:14.220 --> 00:20:16.440
They really don't look like they're in their 50's.

00:20:21.400 --> 00:20:25.320
Geez, how can you think of such
things so early in the morning?!

00:20:23.090 --> 00:20:25.320
Professor, isn't it about that time?

00:20:26.340 --> 00:20:28.600
You know, your famous lame quizzes.

00:20:28.600 --> 00:20:32.410
If you're going to ask us, then do it fast. It's unsettling.

00:20:33.590 --> 00:20:36.960
He's completely being toyed with.

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:42.010
All right, then I'll answer your request
and give the quiz based on this cruise.

00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:47.440
It appears that Genta-kun's received some
treatment at the doctor's office on the ship.

00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:50.470
Now then, what's happened to Genta-kun?

00:20:52.690 --> 00:20:53.480
One.

00:20:53.850 --> 00:20:56.940
He ate too much and hurt his stomach.

00:20:57.270 --> 00:21:00.400
Two. He twisted his ankle after tripping.

00:21:00.830 --> 00:21:05.480
Three. He was out too long in the sun and got heat stroke.

00:21:06.800 --> 00:21:09.250
Now then, what's the right answer?

00:21:10.880 --> 00:21:13.790
If it's the usual Genta-kun,
then it's choice one, but ...

00:21:13.990 --> 00:21:16.660
Nope, it's not the first one.

00:21:16.660 --> 00:21:18.790
I'll never hurt my stomach no matter how much I eat.

00:21:18.990 --> 00:21:20.800
I've got it!

00:21:21.050 --> 00:21:22.300
Me, too.

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:25.730
But isn't that riddle a bit hard for kids?

00:21:25.730 --> 00:21:26.860
Because you have to use English, and ...

00:21:26.860 --> 00:21:28.390
Sonoko!

00:21:28.760 --> 00:21:31.590
English? English is the hint?

00:21:31.590 --> 00:21:33.480
The second hint is "ship".

00:21:33.820 --> 00:21:35.030
Ship?

00:21:36.350 --> 00:21:40.400
I got it, the answer is "2" where he twisted his ankle.

00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:42.480
"Fune" in English is "ship", right?

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:44.610
Genta-kun put a "shippu" on his leg.

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:44.610
Note: a "shippu" is a medicine pack.

00:21:44.920 --> 00:21:46.590
That's correct.

00:21:46.590 --> 00:21:49.060
Just some extra, "Yuujou" is "Friendship".

00:21:49.060 --> 00:21:51.450
"Uwasabanashi" is "Gossip".

00:21:51.450 --> 00:21:54.090
Hey, hey. "Gossip" is different.

00:21:54.540 --> 00:21:56.080
Well then, I'll see you at 10:00 A.M.

00:21:57.740 --> 00:22:00.180
The ship was shippu, huh?

00:22:00.180 --> 00:22:05.130
Hey Mitsuhiko, if I was in a fight while I'm
crossing the ocean, then I'll regret it, right?

00:22:00.180 --> 00:22:05.130
Note: this is another pun, Goukai means crossing he ocean and Koukai means to regret. So it's a play on the sound of the word.

00:22:05.150 --> 00:22:06.520
What the heck is that?

00:22:06.770 --> 00:22:08.480
You think you're so good, huh?

00:22:08.480 --> 00:22:11.930
Oh yeah. When are we going to give it to her?

00:22:11.930 --> 00:22:14.060
We could give it now ...

00:22:14.520 --> 00:22:16.310
Hey, how about something like this?

00:22:19.160 --> 00:22:21.550
Let's go and get the last round of drinks.

00:22:21.550 --> 00:22:22.660
All right.

00:22:23.020 --> 00:22:24.890
We've gotta bring back tons.

00:22:24.890 --> 00:22:26.740
Don't overact about it

00:22:29.800 --> 00:22:31.710
We're going to get some drinks too.

00:22:31.710 --> 00:22:33.630
Let's go and get some!

00:22:33.630 --> 00:22:35.940
What kind of juice should I get?

00:22:38.120 --> 00:22:39.660
Right. Let's go!

00:22:40.060 --> 00:22:40.750
Wait up!

00:22:41.140 --> 00:22:43.250
What are they so excited about?

00:23:11.740 --> 00:23:17.750
I know the secret of 15 years ago.
At 10:15 A.M., come to the basement marina.

00:23:28.710 --> 00:23:34.140
I see. He really did fall from the road
right outside of his mansion.

00:23:36.830 --> 00:23:38.980
Let's go check it out.

00:23:40.750 --> 00:23:44.230
What should we do now?

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:47.690
It's still a bit cold to go for a swim.

00:23:47.690 --> 00:23:49.690
I have to go and change.

00:23:50.530 --> 00:23:51.610
Change?

00:23:53.010 --> 00:23:57.040
I got an invitation from Uruashi Shimai.

00:23:58.400 --> 00:24:02.350
Apparently, she wants to hear the stories
of the great detective Mouri Kogorou.

00:24:02.350 --> 00:24:03.910
Later ...

00:24:04.430 --> 00:24:06.460
He's a real showoff, huh ...

00:24:06.460 --> 00:24:09.050
I wonder when he got the invitation.

00:24:10.450 --> 00:24:11.840
Let's just leave him.

00:24:11.840 --> 00:24:13.430
But what do you all want to do?

00:24:16.070 --> 00:24:17.620
I want to play hide and seek.

00:24:17.620 --> 00:24:19.190
S-Sounds fun.

00:24:19.190 --> 00:24:20.140
Let's do it!

00:24:20.470 --> 00:24:23.190
Hide and seek? How nostalgic.

00:24:23.190 --> 00:24:24.910
We played it a lot when we were kids.

00:24:24.910 --> 00:24:28.030
Yeah. At the park, at my house, and stuff.

00:24:28.340 --> 00:24:30.980
I even played it in elementary school once.

00:24:30.980 --> 00:24:32.400
Oh, really?

00:24:32.950 --> 00:24:34.460
Sorry, but I'll pass.

00:24:35.590 --> 00:24:37.460
Let's play, Conan-kun.

00:24:37.460 --> 00:24:39.160
You're not being part of the group.

00:24:39.160 --> 00:24:42.620
Come to think of it, I think I was
refused by Shinichi at that time, too.

00:24:43.000 --> 00:24:46.040
All right! Let's play hide and seek.

00:24:46.360 --> 00:24:48.800
Well, I suppose it'll kill some time.

00:24:49.110 --> 00:24:50.170
What about you, Professor?

00:24:50.170 --> 00:24:52.540
I have a massage reservation I requested.

00:24:52.540 --> 00:24:54.060
Like an old man.

00:24:54.910 --> 00:24:56.720
Okay, let's decide on the rules.

00:24:57.520 --> 00:24:59.320
The time limit is 30 minutes.

00:24:59.320 --> 00:25:02.000
The hiding area is from the 1st to the 7th floors.

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:05.730
Cabins and employees-only areas are off-limits.

00:25:05.950 --> 00:25:08.210
Same with the bathrooms and the observation room.

00:25:08.210 --> 00:25:09.070
How's that?

00:25:09.500 --> 00:25:10.780
Agreed.

00:25:11.090 --> 00:25:13.650
Well then, everyone. Gather around.

00:25:13.650 --> 00:25:16.660
Rock-Paper-Scissors.

00:25:19.510 --> 00:25:21.240
Sonoko's the seeker!

00:25:19.510 --> 00:25:21.240
Note: in Japanese you would call the seeker "Oni" which in Japanese means monster or demon.

00:25:21.240 --> 00:25:27.390
Hold on, impossible! I can't find six people on a ship this big in 30 minutes!

00:25:27.390 --> 00:25:28.670
Totally impossible.

00:25:29.850 --> 00:25:32.470
Well, let's make another seeker.

00:25:33.030 --> 00:25:34.500
Two seekers?

00:25:34.500 --> 00:25:36.530
Why not? It's different.

00:25:36.530 --> 00:25:38.680
Well then, rock-paper-scissors again.

00:25:42.690 --> 00:25:43.690
I look forward to working with you.

00:25:43.690 --> 00:25:45.020
M-Me, too ...

00:25:45.310 --> 00:25:47.570
Heh, he. Quite an unique combination.

00:25:47.570 --> 00:25:50.860
Oh. Lend me you detective badge.

00:25:50.860 --> 00:25:52.230
Why?

00:25:52.530 --> 00:25:55.820
If there are two seekers, then we won't know who's been caught, right?

00:25:55.820 --> 00:25:58.070
We're going to communicate with those badges.

00:25:58.390 --> 00:26:00.070
Fine. Don't lose it.

00:26:00.290 --> 00:26:03.930
Well then, we'll start at 9:50 A.M. So ...

00:26:03.930 --> 00:26:07.790
if the seekers find everyone by
10:20 A.M. then the seekers win.

00:26:08.000 --> 00:26:09.960
Okay, I won't lose!

00:26:11.130 --> 00:26:13.880
Too bad, but we'll win because ...

00:26:14.190 --> 00:26:16.560
We've got Conan-kun.

00:26:16.560 --> 00:26:18.340
Even if you say that ...

00:26:18.340 --> 00:26:20.000
All right, let's go.

00:26:20.000 --> 00:26:21.810
Hide and seek... Start!

00:26:21.810 --> 00:26:23.680
Yay!

00:26:24.010 --> 00:26:25.020
Later.

00:26:25.020 --> 00:26:26.650
We'll start in five minutes.

00:26:29.070 --> 00:26:31.450
Ran-oneesan didn't notice it.

00:26:31.450 --> 00:26:33.940
She'll surely notice it while we're playing.

00:26:33.940 --> 00:26:36.070
She'll be so surprised!

00:26:39.920 --> 00:26:40.670
All right.

00:26:40.670 --> 00:26:41.780
I got it!

00:26:44.380 --> 00:26:46.000
I guess this isn't a good place.

00:26:47.360 --> 00:26:49.300
When was the movie?

00:26:49.300 --> 00:26:50.880
Wasn't it at 10:00 A.M.?

00:26:52.650 --> 00:26:53.810
We should get going.

00:26:53.810 --> 00:26:54.630
Hurry!

00:26:54.630 --> 00:26:55.660
It's gonna start.

00:27:13.310 --> 00:27:14.770
That was close.

00:27:22.200 --> 00:27:22.820
All right!

00:27:40.000 --> 00:27:43.010
Who would have thought that I'd be the seeker?

00:27:43.370 --> 00:27:47.020
But, I suppose it's nice to be
on the seeking side for once.

00:27:48.110 --> 00:27:49.390
Five minutes have passed.

00:27:49.670 --> 00:27:52.980
I'll look from floor five and up.
I'll leave the bottom to you, okay?

00:27:53.570 --> 00:27:55.120
S-Sure ...

00:27:58.950 --> 00:28:00.650
Hey, Kudou-kun.

00:28:01.060 --> 00:28:02.470
Hey, Haibara.

00:28:03.860 --> 00:28:07.120
You know, I don't think you understand
the meaning of hide and seek.

00:28:14.100 --> 00:28:15.570
Got one.

00:28:16.550 --> 00:28:18.880
Darn. How did you know?

00:28:18.880 --> 00:28:22.470
The ones who eat a lot have always hidden at the cafeteria since the old days.

00:28:33.480 --> 00:28:35.770
Whoa! Haibara-san ...

00:28:36.610 --> 00:28:38.360
I'm guessing you borrowed that from the Professor.

00:28:38.900 --> 00:28:41.360
You need to hide where it fits in.

00:28:42.080 --> 00:28:43.900
Hey. Come out.

00:28:43.900 --> 00:28:47.780
Ah, man. I thought it was a good hiding place.

00:28:48.000 --> 00:28:52.190
Nope. You're still ten years too early to beat me.

00:29:01.540 --> 00:29:03.220
Hello. This is Akiyoshi.

00:29:03.520 --> 00:29:05.750
Hello, Minako-san? It's Kusaka.

00:29:05.750 --> 00:29:06.470
Yes.

00:29:06.960 --> 00:29:10.180
Well, then. To get right to the point,

00:29:10.830 --> 00:29:13.390
Okazaki Nanami, age 20.

00:29:13.390 --> 00:29:16.190
An attendant on the luxury cruise St. Sazan Cross.

00:29:26.190 --> 00:29:28.780
All right, I'm going to read the story.

00:29:32.660 --> 00:29:39.200
Okazaki Nanami loved the ocean ever since she was born.

00:29:39.550 --> 00:29:43.090
She loved its vastness more than anything else.

00:30:40.990 --> 00:30:43.230
We managed to find these four pretty easily, but ...

00:30:43.830 --> 00:30:46.740
The hardest one turned out to be the last as suspected.

00:30:47.580 --> 00:30:50.110
Ran-san's really good at hiding?

00:30:50.330 --> 00:30:52.430
She's like a ninja, a ninja!

00:30:52.430 --> 00:30:56.870
Does an ordinary elementary kid
climb on ceilings and dive in ponds?

00:30:56.870 --> 00:30:58.550
Ceilings ...

00:30:58.550 --> 00:31:00.770
Inside ponds ...

00:31:01.570 --> 00:31:03.010
Wow ...

00:31:05.050 --> 00:31:08.800
Haha. She's had a lot of
stamina since she was younger.

00:31:10.250 --> 00:31:12.800
We still have 12 minutes. Let's find her.

00:31:24.780 --> 00:31:26.870
This place isn't it, either.

00:31:27.790 --> 00:31:29.530
10:11 A.M.

00:31:29.810 --> 00:31:32.650
Geez, there are only nine minutes left.

00:31:52.360 --> 00:31:54.890
Sorry to keep you waiting. It's me, Mouri!

00:32:08.500 --> 00:32:09.960
I'm taking revenge for my father!

00:32:57.630 --> 00:32:58.990
I'm starting the countdown.

00:32:59.250 --> 00:33:00.240
5...

00:33:00.530 --> 00:33:01.250
4...

00:33:01.570 --> 00:33:02.250
3...

00:33:02.560 --> 00:33:03.250
2...

00:33:03.540 --> 00:33:04.250
1...

00:33:04.520 --> 00:33:05.430
Zero!

00:33:05.430 --> 00:33:07.590
We win hide and seek!

00:33:09.110 --> 00:33:10.690
It's all thanks to ninja Ran-san.

00:33:10.690 --> 00:33:12.140
Yeah, yeah.

00:33:12.140 --> 00:33:13.050
Ran-oneesan!

00:33:14.130 --> 00:33:16.430
I told you we'd win.

00:33:16.690 --> 00:33:19.090
Where were you hiding, Ran-neechan?

00:33:19.090 --> 00:33:23.640
You were kicking the soccer ball
the entire time, right? I knew it all along.

00:33:24.330 --> 00:33:27.020
It doesn't look like Ran-oneesan found it yet.

00:33:27.020 --> 00:33:28.520
That's strange.

00:33:28.520 --> 00:33:30.020
Maybe she's just slow.

00:33:30.440 --> 00:33:32.820
I wonder if she's still looking?

00:33:38.640 --> 00:33:43.240
Wha... So cold! What is this?

00:33:46.780 --> 00:33:49.180
A box? Am I in an box?

00:33:54.390 --> 00:33:58.570
No ... Someone ... Someone help!

00:34:01.510 --> 00:34:04.330
Help! Somebody, help me!

00:34:04.330 --> 00:34:06.850
What's wrong, Sonoko-neechan?

00:34:07.350 --> 00:34:08.900
Help!

00:34:09.570 --> 00:34:11.480
Calm down Sonoko, where are you?

00:34:12.760 --> 00:34:16.750
I'm in a box somewhere ...

00:34:16.750 --> 00:34:19.630
I can't hear you, Sonoko, say that again!

00:34:24.540 --> 00:34:26.340
Are the batteries dead?

00:34:29.460 --> 00:34:31.650
Shit, back there ...

00:34:31.650 --> 00:34:35.280
You're cold, Sonoko? It's cold?

00:34:35.760 --> 00:34:37.380
She's shivering.

00:34:38.290 --> 00:34:39.720
It's the freezer!

00:34:43.580 --> 00:34:45.140
Hey! What are you guys doing?

00:34:45.470 --> 00:34:47.110
Where's your freezer?

00:34:47.110 --> 00:34:48.150
Freezer?

00:34:48.150 --> 00:34:50.480
Please, my friend is in trouble!

00:34:50.880 --> 00:34:52.870
It's on the second basement floor.

00:34:58.530 --> 00:35:00.140
There are so many!

00:35:00.140 --> 00:35:00.910
Which one is it?

00:35:01.270 --> 00:35:02.780
Let's split up and find her.

00:35:02.780 --> 00:35:03.550
Yes.

00:35:04.830 --> 00:35:06.410
Sonoko-neechan!

00:35:08.700 --> 00:35:10.000
Sonoko-san.

00:35:10.410 --> 00:35:12.960
Sonoko! Are you here?

00:35:13.170 --> 00:35:15.840
Sonoko-oneesan, where are you?!

00:35:16.540 --> 00:35:19.030
It doesn't look like she's here. Let's go outside.

00:35:20.930 --> 00:35:23.290
That was cold.

00:35:23.290 --> 00:35:25.260
Sonoko, Sonoko! Answer me, Sonoko!

00:35:25.460 --> 00:35:28.730
Damn it! Where? Where is she?

00:35:28.990 --> 00:35:31.920
Hey, maybe she's already dead ...

00:35:31.920 --> 00:35:34.040
Don't say such things!

00:35:34.040 --> 00:35:38.160
But there isn't any other place that's cold, is there?

00:35:38.480 --> 00:35:40.060
Dead ...

00:35:40.870 --> 00:35:41.740
It's there!

00:35:42.540 --> 00:35:44.740
This ship has a place like this?

00:35:45.320 --> 00:35:47.240
It's a little bizarre, huh?

00:35:49.790 --> 00:35:51.000
It's heavy.

00:35:55.440 --> 00:35:56.620
Sonoko!

00:36:00.530 --> 00:36:02.000
Sonoko ...

00:36:02.000 --> 00:36:03.760
Let's get her to the infirmary.

00:36:06.610 --> 00:36:09.270
Ha ... I'm alive again.

00:36:09.500 --> 00:36:11.080
There's no need to worry.

00:36:11.080 --> 00:36:16.020
Once she warms her body and relaxes,
she should be able to move soon.

00:36:16.360 --> 00:36:18.140
Thank you.

00:36:18.140 --> 00:36:19.940
Isn't that great, Sonoko?

00:36:20.610 --> 00:36:21.700
But ...

00:36:21.700 --> 00:36:23.450
Who would pull a prank like this?

00:36:23.940 --> 00:36:27.090
Prank? This is no prank.

00:36:27.090 --> 00:36:29.160
It's an official murder attempt.

00:36:29.550 --> 00:36:31.240
Please call the police immediately.

00:36:31.240 --> 00:36:33.080
Y-Yes, sir.

00:36:34.650 --> 00:36:37.210
Tell me the story.

00:36:37.210 --> 00:36:38.380
Where were you attacked?

00:36:38.790 --> 00:36:41.460
At the marina. I went to look for Ran,

00:36:41.460 --> 00:36:44.390
then I was suddenly hit on
the shoulder by a stick or something,

00:36:44.390 --> 00:36:46.390
And I think I lost consciousness from there.

00:36:46.390 --> 00:36:48.180
What about the face of the attacker?

00:36:48.420 --> 00:36:52.460
Hmm. I think I saw it, but I don't remember.

00:36:52.460 --> 00:36:53.410
What about the time?

00:36:53.410 --> 00:36:56.520
Oh, I remember that. It was at 10:11 A.M.

00:36:57.390 --> 00:36:59.200
10:11 A.M.

00:37:02.050 --> 00:37:06.950
I see. From here, the mortuary is only feet away.

00:37:06.950 --> 00:37:10.790
But why was Sonoko-neechan attacked?

00:37:19.930 --> 00:37:20.590
This is ...

00:37:21.140 --> 00:37:23.430
President Yashiro's metallic fan.

00:37:23.430 --> 00:37:25.590
Why would it be in a place like this?

00:37:30.140 --> 00:37:30.990
No one's here.

00:37:30.990 --> 00:37:33.860
Mouri-san! The captain said that the police ...

00:37:36.430 --> 00:37:38.770
This is President Yashiro's room.

00:37:38.950 --> 00:37:41.900
Yeah, I heard from Uruashi Shimai earlier.

00:37:42.940 --> 00:37:46.280
Come to think of it, someone came out of this room.

00:37:46.760 --> 00:37:48.170
Who?

00:37:48.520 --> 00:37:50.050
I didn't see the person's face ...

00:37:51.140 --> 00:37:54.540
Whoever it was wore a windbreaker and a hood ...

00:37:55.020 --> 00:37:56.120
What time?

00:37:56.370 --> 00:37:59.260
I think it was about 10:15 A.M.

00:37:59.260 --> 00:38:00.750
Really, Mouri-san?

00:38:01.370 --> 00:38:05.630
That's strange. Neither of them wear a windbreaker,

00:38:06.120 --> 00:38:09.810
And at that time, only Chief Takae should have been here.

00:38:13.100 --> 00:38:16.470
Hey. Wearing a windbreaker hood in the hallway,

00:38:16.470 --> 00:38:19.310
isn't that like the person was
trying to hide his or her face?

00:38:20.650 --> 00:38:22.470
Could something have happened to the Chief?

00:38:22.470 --> 00:38:25.700
Chief! It's Tsujimoto. Chief!

00:38:25.700 --> 00:38:27.880
Hey, you have a master key, right?

00:38:27.880 --> 00:38:28.880
But ...

00:38:28.880 --> 00:38:30.370
Chief, excuse me for intruding.

00:38:39.100 --> 00:38:39.880
Chief!

00:38:39.880 --> 00:38:41.780
Don't move! Stay here.

00:38:51.410 --> 00:38:52.520
That can't be ...

00:38:52.520 --> 00:38:53.720
Who in the world ...

00:38:53.720 --> 00:38:57.020
About 30 minutes have passed since she died.

00:38:57.020 --> 00:38:58.500
I'll go and tell the captain.

00:38:58.500 --> 00:39:00.180
I'll go to the President.

00:39:02.580 --> 00:39:05.610
It looks like she was stabbed
when she came out of the bathroom.

00:39:12.270 --> 00:39:14.560
The blood on this side has been wiped clean.

00:39:14.560 --> 00:39:15.550
But why?

00:39:16.410 --> 00:39:17.790
Why only the blood on this side ...

00:39:20.520 --> 00:39:22.130
What the heck are you doing?

00:39:23.590 --> 00:39:24.500
Ouch ...

00:39:25.030 --> 00:39:25.880
Geez.

00:39:26.310 --> 00:39:27.400
Mouri-san!

00:39:28.660 --> 00:39:30.440
About President Yashiro.

00:39:30.440 --> 00:39:33.890
Niemi-san says he never came back
after he left the billiard room.

00:39:34.230 --> 00:39:35.850
What?!

00:39:37.110 --> 00:39:42.190
President Yashiro may have gotten
into some trouble as well.

00:40:04.310 --> 00:40:05.220
Thanks for coming.

00:40:05.220 --> 00:40:06.050
Mouri-san.

00:40:06.050 --> 00:40:07.990
Thank you for coming, Chief Inspector.

00:40:08.830 --> 00:40:10.460
Have you located President Yashiro?

00:40:10.460 --> 00:40:12.680
We still don't know where he is.

00:40:12.680 --> 00:40:16.640
The crew split up and searched the entire ship, but ...

00:40:16.920 --> 00:40:21.890
In the air or on the waters, cases follow
you wherever you go, Mouri-san.

00:40:22.090 --> 00:40:23.720
Will it be space next time?

00:40:23.720 --> 00:40:25.190
Going to get on some rocket?

00:40:25.500 --> 00:40:27.570
Of course not!

00:40:44.270 --> 00:40:46.840
What? The President's fingerprints?

00:40:47.070 --> 00:40:52.300
Yes, they were focused around the area where traces of blood were discovered at the marina.

00:40:52.300 --> 00:40:57.970
Of course, the blood found on the exit door also matched that of President Yashiro.

00:40:58.240 --> 00:41:01.980
Thank you. Keep up the good work.

00:41:01.980 --> 00:41:03.300
Also, Chief Inspector.

00:41:03.300 --> 00:41:05.670
According to the marina employees,

00:41:05.670 --> 00:41:09.920
Those doors appeared to have been opened.

00:41:09.920 --> 00:41:11.280
Furthermore, they were opened recently.

00:41:11.510 --> 00:41:12.360
What?

00:41:14.270 --> 00:41:17.840
The fingerprints, the traces of blood, the door's lock.

00:41:18.310 --> 00:41:20.100
Chief Inspector, this looks like ...

00:41:20.100 --> 00:41:24.480
It looks like President Yashiro was
attacked by someone in the marina,

00:41:24.480 --> 00:41:27.330
And was thrown into the ocean through the door.

00:41:28.000 --> 00:41:30.300
I believe we can safely assume that.

00:41:30.460 --> 00:41:32.000
Indeed.

00:41:32.000 --> 00:41:37.140
Shiratori-kun, contact the coast guard
and ask for a sweep of the immediate area.

00:41:37.140 --> 00:41:38.310
Understood.

00:41:38.310 --> 00:41:39.240
Takagi-kun.

00:41:39.240 --> 00:41:40.060
Yes.

00:41:40.350 --> 00:41:42.850
I want to talk to the Niemi couple as well.

00:41:42.850 --> 00:41:43.810
Bring them to me.

00:41:43.810 --> 00:41:44.400
Yes, sir.

00:41:47.600 --> 00:41:49.280
Now then, Conan-kun.

00:41:49.280 --> 00:41:50.320
Yes?

00:41:50.570 --> 00:41:52.520
Leave the rest to us.

00:41:52.520 --> 00:41:54.190
I want you to return to your room.

00:41:54.570 --> 00:41:57.730
Don't go outside unnecessarily.

00:41:57.730 --> 00:42:01.160
There's a high chance that the murderer is still on this ship.

00:42:01.410 --> 00:42:02.750
Okay.

00:42:09.940 --> 00:42:11.770
Wow, there's a cake, too!

00:42:11.770 --> 00:42:13.390
It looks delicious.

00:42:15.300 --> 00:42:17.220
Roast beef ...

00:42:20.860 --> 00:42:23.040
I suppose occasionally it's fine ...

00:42:25.870 --> 00:42:27.260
Not even occasionally.

00:42:28.620 --> 00:42:29.760
Oh Professor,

00:42:29.760 --> 00:42:32.960
Should we bring Ran-san
and Sonoko-san's meals too?

00:42:33.200 --> 00:42:35.190
I'm sure they're hungry, too.

00:42:35.430 --> 00:42:38.950
No, we should let the doctors take care of Sonoko-kun.

00:42:39.290 --> 00:42:42.980
Ran-oneesan said that she would eat
later so don't worry about it.

00:42:42.980 --> 00:42:44.140
I see ...

00:42:44.140 --> 00:42:45.490
Hey Mitsuhiko,

00:42:45.490 --> 00:42:47.160
do you think she found the gold medal?

00:42:47.540 --> 00:42:50.110
I don't think Ran-san has had the time
to think about something like that.

00:42:50.110 --> 00:42:51.250
I thought so ...

00:42:51.250 --> 00:42:53.050
Where's Conan-kun?

00:42:53.330 --> 00:42:55.380
Come to think of it, he's not here.

00:42:55.790 --> 00:43:00.090
Maybe he sneaked out to listen
to the police investigation!

00:43:00.450 --> 00:43:02.100
Probably.

00:43:02.100 --> 00:43:05.470
It seems he's good at that kind of hide and seek

00:43:05.850 --> 00:43:08.100
Thank you for your cooperation.

00:43:08.990 --> 00:43:12.980
I probably don't need to say this,
but please catch the culprit as soon as possible.

00:43:12.980 --> 00:43:13.740
Yes, sir!

00:43:20.310 --> 00:43:21.490
Now, then.

00:43:22.000 --> 00:43:27.500
If we assume that Chief Takae was murdered right after she returned to her room from her squash game and took a bath,

00:43:27.950 --> 00:43:34.550
I believe we can safely say that the person wearing the windbreaker that Mouri-kun saw leaving her room was the culprit.

00:43:35.400 --> 00:43:39.970
If that culprit went down to the basement marina afterwards,

00:43:39.970 --> 00:43:43.970
and murdered President Yashiro,
who got called out earlier ...

00:43:44.250 --> 00:43:46.430
Then it would be just right time-wise as well.

00:43:46.430 --> 00:43:52.410
Meaning that these two cases were most likely done by the same individual.

00:43:55.030 --> 00:43:57.570
Mouri-kun, what about the culprit's characteristics?

00:43:57.940 --> 00:44:00.780
The height was about 170 cm.

00:44:00.780 --> 00:44:02.950
And it was a fairly skinny individual.

00:44:03.260 --> 00:44:07.420
With just the height, we can't be certain whether it was a male or female.

00:44:07.420 --> 00:44:12.700
Come to think of it, the murdered Chief Takae
was about the same height as well.

00:44:14.060 --> 00:44:16.260
Tsujimoto-san, is that the ...

00:44:16.260 --> 00:44:16.840
Yes.

00:44:17.280 --> 00:44:21.720
As a complimentary item for being on
this ship, we gave one to each guest.

00:44:21.870 --> 00:44:26.650
But if they really wanted to, the crew
could have gotten a hold of one, right?

00:44:27.940 --> 00:44:30.780
Shiratori-kun, what about the culprit's motives?

00:44:30.780 --> 00:44:33.440
I believe we can say it was a grudge.

00:44:33.980 --> 00:44:37.320
The victim's jewelry and wallet were never touched.

00:44:37.800 --> 00:44:41.450
There was no trace of the lock being picked.

00:44:41.450 --> 00:44:44.820
Either the victim herself invited the culprit in,

00:44:45.340 --> 00:44:49.290
or the culprit used a master key of some sort and sneaked in.

00:44:49.290 --> 00:44:52.820
Misaki-san, who holds the master keys?

00:44:52.820 --> 00:44:54.830
There are quite a few.

00:44:55.220 --> 00:44:57.320
I, of course, as a security officer.

00:44:57.320 --> 00:44:59.070
The house assistant, Natsuho-kun.

00:44:59.070 --> 00:45:03.220
And the chief cabin attendants all have one.

00:45:03.570 --> 00:45:04.980
I see ...

00:45:04.980 --> 00:45:09.430
Chief Inspector, the culprit targeted the victim when she was alone.

00:45:09.900 --> 00:45:14.440
If that's the case, then perhaps the culprit knew the victim's schedule.

00:45:16.750 --> 00:45:21.760
Tsujimoto-san, you arranged their schedules, is that right?

00:45:21.760 --> 00:45:22.490
Yes.

00:45:23.070 --> 00:45:26.080
Who else knew about them?

00:45:26.080 --> 00:45:28.930
I told the chief purser, Misaki-san,

00:45:29.440 --> 00:45:31.370
but never told anyone else.

00:45:33.130 --> 00:45:33.870
Meaning,

00:45:34.260 --> 00:45:37.040
if you were 10 cm taller,

00:45:37.040 --> 00:45:39.790
or if Misaki-san's weight was 10 kg less,

00:45:39.790 --> 00:45:41.970
one of you would have become the prime suspect.

00:45:44.000 --> 00:45:45.610
Also, one more thing.

00:45:45.610 --> 00:45:50.560
Whether Sonoko-kun's case has
anything to do with these two cases.

00:45:52.050 --> 00:45:57.860
But to pass by someone who may have been the culprit and not to have seen their face ...

00:45:58.570 --> 00:46:00.420
I'm very sorry.

00:46:00.420 --> 00:46:02.230
Anyhow, Chief Inspector ...

00:46:02.230 --> 00:46:04.420
This place is a closed room above the ocean.

00:46:04.420 --> 00:46:07.410
The murderer is definitely somewhere on this ship.

00:46:07.750 --> 00:46:12.660
The crew and the guests, all together,
 it's only 600 suspects, right?

00:46:14.550 --> 00:46:15.970
Anyway, Takagi-kun,

00:46:15.970 --> 00:46:19.020
continue your questioning with
the guests and find a witness.

00:46:19.020 --> 00:46:19.860
Yes, sir!

00:46:20.260 --> 00:46:21.880
Misaki-san and Tsujimoto-san,

00:46:22.350 --> 00:46:25.090
Please tell us thoroughly about
each guest and crew member.

00:46:25.090 --> 00:46:26.370
Understood.

00:46:28.470 --> 00:46:31.220
It's exactly as Officer Shiratori said.

00:46:31.220 --> 00:46:34.320
The culprit knew about the Yashiro family's schedule.

00:46:35.550 --> 00:46:38.220
Natsuho-san says she didn't tell anyone.

00:46:39.540 --> 00:46:40.810
That's ...

00:46:41.410 --> 00:46:44.320
I see! If one used that ...

00:46:45.040 --> 00:46:48.280
Hey, hey! I have something to ask you, Oneesan.

00:46:49.050 --> 00:46:50.040
Conan-kun?

00:46:50.040 --> 00:46:52.660
Hey! Where did you come from?

00:46:57.160 --> 00:47:01.600
Last night, didn't you talk about today's schedule in the President's room?

00:47:01.600 --> 00:47:06.720
Yes, after we had dinner and
came back to the suite.

00:47:06.980 --> 00:47:11.400
Then, was there any time yesterday
when no one was in the President's room?

00:47:11.400 --> 00:47:18.660
Let's see, yesterday, President Yashiro said
he was tired, so he was resting until dinner ...

00:47:18.660 --> 00:47:21.730
The only time the room was empty was during dinner.

00:47:22.050 --> 00:47:23.270
I see ...

00:47:23.270 --> 00:47:25.200
You little!

00:47:26.040 --> 00:47:29.860
You were listening to the conversation, weren't you?

00:47:32.300 --> 00:47:34.620
Ouch!

00:47:35.680 --> 00:47:38.960
Misaki-san, was there anyone
that didn't show up to dinner?

00:47:39.350 --> 00:47:42.460
No, I believe everyone came.

00:47:44.020 --> 00:47:46.460
Then the culprit should be one of the crew members.

00:47:48.360 --> 00:47:52.430
Sorry, I'm going to leave now and rest in my room.

00:47:55.080 --> 00:47:58.730
Hey, have you ever participated
 in Kusaka-san's research?

00:47:59.060 --> 00:48:02.100
Kusaka Hironari-san? Yes, I have.

00:48:02.100 --> 00:48:05.700
Did a master key go missing after that by any chance?

00:48:06.820 --> 00:48:09.820
Enough already, of course not!

00:48:10.350 --> 00:48:15.990
Actually, about three weeks ago,
we realized that one had gone missing.

00:48:15.990 --> 00:48:17.240
What... There is...?

00:48:17.480 --> 00:48:22.000
Further more, it was right after I participated in Kusaka-san's research, just as Conan-kun said.

00:48:22.000 --> 00:48:26.630
Hold on. Who is this Kusaka-san?

00:48:26.800 --> 00:48:30.630
He's a script writer who has come here for research purposes a few times.

00:48:30.870 --> 00:48:32.330
I see ...

00:48:32.330 --> 00:48:36.350
So, Conan-kun. Are there any
suspicious points to that person?

00:48:36.350 --> 00:48:40.500
Yeah. Kusaka-san returned to
his room in the middle of dinner.

00:48:40.500 --> 00:48:42.230
Saying he got seasick.

00:48:42.490 --> 00:48:47.540
But maybe he was hiding in the
President's room and eavesdropping.

00:48:47.540 --> 00:48:51.740
Idiot. He's not a kid, so he won't do
some hide and seek stuff like that ...

00:48:51.930 --> 00:48:53.030
Wire tapping.

00:48:55.170 --> 00:48:59.130
Maybe he left a tapping device in the President's room.

00:48:59.130 --> 00:49:04.210
I see, how about it, Mouri-kun?
What's Kusaka-san's physical stature?

00:49:04.760 --> 00:49:08.000
Now that you mention it,
it does resemble the culprit's.

00:49:08.260 --> 00:49:10.960
All right, let's go to see Kusaka-san.

00:49:16.310 --> 00:49:18.970
I see, a tapping device.

00:49:19.580 --> 00:49:22.390
You're indeed the great detective Mouri Kogorou.

00:49:22.750 --> 00:49:26.400
Actually, this time it was thanks to Conan-kun's idea,

00:49:26.630 --> 00:49:28.390
And we did a bit of reasoning.

00:49:29.400 --> 00:49:31.710
Really?

00:49:31.710 --> 00:49:33.780
But that reasoning is wrong.

00:49:34.030 --> 00:49:36.550
Around 10:15 A.M.,

00:49:36.550 --> 00:49:39.390
I was on the phone with Minako-san in this room.

00:49:40.530 --> 00:49:42.580
You mean the designer Minako-san?

00:49:42.990 --> 00:49:47.560
Yes, because we're on the ocean,
I couldn't use my cell phone.

00:49:47.560 --> 00:49:48.630
So I was using this phone right here.

00:49:49.050 --> 00:49:50.630
The exact time you were on the phone?

00:49:50.910 --> 00:49:54.380
Let's see, from about 10:00 until 10:30 A.M.

00:49:54.850 --> 00:49:56.640
If you check the calling record,

00:49:56.640 --> 00:49:59.080
I think you'll get the exact time.

00:50:00.160 --> 00:50:02.460
And what was the phone call about?

00:50:03.010 --> 00:50:04.430
If you don't mind.

00:50:05.450 --> 00:50:09.190
I was done with the script draft,
so I thought of having her listen to it.

00:50:09.390 --> 00:50:10.830
The script draft?

00:50:11.190 --> 00:50:16.030
Yes, the draft for a drama series
set on an luxury cruise liner.

00:50:16.340 --> 00:50:19.490
I've been receiving advise from her about cruise ships.

00:50:28.810 --> 00:50:31.130
Cruising Love Story?

00:50:31.850 --> 00:50:33.860
I specifically asked for an open room alone,

00:50:33.860 --> 00:50:37.590
so that I could finish this without
being disturbed by anyone else.

00:50:37.880 --> 00:50:41.010
But why didn't you see her
in person and talk to her about it?

00:50:41.010 --> 00:50:42.780
You're both on the same ship.

00:50:43.160 --> 00:50:47.270
She's still single, so to go to her room is a little ...

00:50:47.820 --> 00:50:51.820
And at a cafe or a lounge,
there is a chance someone will hear us.

00:50:52.440 --> 00:50:56.190
It happens a lot in my career.
Stealing ideas, I mean.

00:50:56.440 --> 00:50:58.150
I see ...

00:51:03.280 --> 00:51:06.620
From what I can see, Kusaka-san is clear.

00:51:07.030 --> 00:51:11.080
We don't know yet, not until we can confirm his alibi.

00:51:20.820 --> 00:51:22.300
What's wrong, Mouri-san?

00:51:24.380 --> 00:51:26.610
He was probably caught on that lady there.

00:51:26.610 --> 00:51:28.440
She was pretty cute, so ...

00:51:35.110 --> 00:51:37.860
I heard about the case from Misaki-san.

00:51:38.260 --> 00:51:42.120
It's true that at precisely 10:00 A.M.,
I received a call from Kusaka-san.

00:51:42.120 --> 00:51:44.110
And we talked for about 30 minutes.

00:51:45.090 --> 00:51:48.020
He's been asking me to review his work,

00:51:48.020 --> 00:51:49.990
So this morning, during tea time,

00:51:49.990 --> 00:51:53.590
He said, "The story will be finished soon,
so I want to hear what you think about it".

00:51:53.970 --> 00:51:58.090
"I'll call you at 10:00 A.M.,
so please be in your room at that time."

00:51:58.540 --> 00:52:02.460
I see. Well, as long as we can confirm that.

00:52:02.460 --> 00:52:04.050
Sorry to bother you.

00:52:15.390 --> 00:52:18.320
I guess Mr. Kusaka's alibi is confirmed.

00:52:18.320 --> 00:52:21.820
Yes, as long as the two aren't working together.

00:52:22.210 --> 00:52:24.950
The phone isn't wireless in their rooms.

00:52:25.270 --> 00:52:28.950
It's impossible to commit the crime as they talk on the phone.

00:52:33.030 --> 00:52:34.540
What's up, Mouri-san?

00:52:36.330 --> 00:52:38.840
You were probably thinking about Minako-san, right?

00:52:38.840 --> 00:52:41.010
She's pretty good looking, too.

00:52:45.510 --> 00:52:47.470
- From the above ...
- Tome-san.

00:52:47.470 --> 00:52:48.860
Chief Inspector Megure.

00:52:48.860 --> 00:52:49.970
How is it?

00:52:50.310 --> 00:52:52.090
We've finished going over it once,

00:52:52.090 --> 00:52:54.330
But there isn't really anything that jumps out.

00:52:54.330 --> 00:52:55.610
I see.

00:52:55.820 --> 00:53:01.570
Just that there were traces of a reddish yellow substance that were wiped off on the floor near the body.

00:53:01.570 --> 00:53:03.360
A reddish-yellow substance?

00:53:03.710 --> 00:53:06.030
Hey, Tome-san, that wasn't blood?

00:53:06.350 --> 00:53:10.620
No. It's got the same color,
but it didn't respond like blood.

00:53:10.950 --> 00:53:12.290
Then what was it?

00:53:14.030 --> 00:53:15.120
Chief Inspector Megure.

00:53:16.330 --> 00:53:20.050
I've talked to all the guests and
crew members on the sixth floor,

00:53:20.500 --> 00:53:22.750
But still haven't found any witnesses.

00:53:22.750 --> 00:53:24.250
I see ...

00:53:25.340 --> 00:53:28.050
The welcome party starts at 5:00 P.M.

00:53:28.460 --> 00:53:32.950
Let's split up and ask the other
guests on the ship as well.

00:53:32.950 --> 00:53:33.560
Yes, sir!

00:53:33.560 --> 00:53:35.410
Well then, Chief Inspector.

00:53:35.410 --> 00:53:39.020
We will be heading back to HQ
with the evidence we've collected.

00:53:39.270 --> 00:53:41.110
Thanks for your work.

00:53:53.650 --> 00:53:55.080
Oneesan.

00:53:56.720 --> 00:53:59.540
I've been looking for you.
Can I ask you one more question?

00:54:00.010 --> 00:54:02.380
Sure thing, little detective.

00:54:02.380 --> 00:54:03.720
What is it?

00:54:04.020 --> 00:54:06.840
What was the phone call
between you and Kusaka-san like?

00:54:06.840 --> 00:54:14.350
Well... He was reading his story
 and I was just listening.

00:54:14.660 --> 00:54:16.270
You were just listening?

00:54:16.540 --> 00:54:20.180
Yes. If I interrupt in the middle, he gets angry ...

00:54:20.180 --> 00:54:22.460
He would tell me, "Stay quiet and listen".

00:54:23.730 --> 00:54:29.160
Something like that happened before,
so I decided not to interrupt him.

00:54:29.160 --> 00:54:33.660
Then you were just listening silently
until he finished his story?

00:54:34.200 --> 00:54:39.580
Yes. He finished reading his story in about
20 minutes and asked me how it was.

00:54:39.960 --> 00:54:42.190
So I replied it was good.

00:54:44.030 --> 00:54:45.070
Done!

00:54:45.810 --> 00:54:46.590
Here.

00:54:46.590 --> 00:54:48.490
Oh... Thank you ...

00:54:55.540 --> 00:54:57.600
How are you feeling, Sonoko?

00:54:57.910 --> 00:54:59.600
I'm fine now.

00:54:59.600 --> 00:55:03.040
Maybe it would have been better if
we hadn't played hide and seek.

00:55:03.040 --> 00:55:04.730
Not at all.

00:55:04.730 --> 00:55:06.950
But right before we played hide and seek, you said,

00:55:08.140 --> 00:55:10.610
We're going to win this. Because ...

00:55:11.320 --> 00:55:13.280
What were you going to say after that?

00:55:14.570 --> 00:55:17.510
I told you that I played hide and seek once during elementary school, right?

00:55:17.510 --> 00:55:18.290
Yeah.

00:55:18.880 --> 00:55:22.880
That was during the school field
expansion when I was in first grade.

00:55:22.880 --> 00:55:25.660
I invited Shinichi at the time too, but ...

00:55:27.010 --> 00:55:29.680
Shinichi, are you listening to me?

00:55:29.900 --> 00:55:31.100
Come on, Shinichi.

00:55:31.100 --> 00:55:32.610
Let's play hide and seek.

00:55:32.610 --> 00:55:33.930
It's fun.

00:55:34.320 --> 00:55:35.830
Sorry, but I'll pass.

00:55:36.990 --> 00:55:38.950
The soccer tournament is coming up.

00:55:38.950 --> 00:55:40.560
That spoiled brat.

00:55:40.940 --> 00:55:43.440
He's been saying stuff like that since he was a kid?

00:55:43.900 --> 00:55:46.690
And we decided to play without Shinichi.

00:55:46.690 --> 00:55:50.450
But you remember how the area under the
stage in the gym was used as storage?

00:55:50.710 --> 00:55:53.450
Oh, yeah! The folding chairs were stored there, right?

00:55:53.740 --> 00:55:59.570
Yeah. And on the side of the stage, under the stairs, there was a small space there as well.

00:56:03.770 --> 00:56:05.670
So you hid there ...

00:56:05.890 --> 00:56:09.400
Yeah. I thought that if I hid there
no one would ever find me.

00:56:09.400 --> 00:56:14.080
Then the teacher who came to check things out
put the stairs back and I got stuck inside.

00:56:15.060 --> 00:56:16.410
And then...?

00:56:16.990 --> 00:56:19.660
No matter how hard everyone looked, they couldn't find me.

00:56:19.660 --> 00:56:22.560
And I couldn't get out so I was wondering what to do.

00:56:22.560 --> 00:56:25.690
But then, Shinichi found me easily.

00:56:28.400 --> 00:56:33.590
On the way home, I asked him how
he knew where I was and he said ...

00:56:33.590 --> 00:56:35.070
"The Demons of the School."

00:56:36.530 --> 00:56:42.020
In that movie, the kids who hid in the school building were all eaten by the demon, right?

00:56:42.020 --> 00:56:45.680
That means, the chance of you hiding in any of the school buildings would be zero.

00:56:45.680 --> 00:56:49.800
Wait a sec, how did you know I watched that movie?

00:56:49.800 --> 00:56:54.830
Every time we passed the video store,
you always looked at that movie poster.

00:56:54.830 --> 00:56:59.340
Even though you're afraid of ghosts and demons, you always watch those movies.

00:57:01.510 --> 00:57:05.060
That means you were hiding somewhere in the outer school buildings.

00:57:05.060 --> 00:57:09.980
You, an animal lover, wouldn't hide in the hen house where you'd scare all the chickens.

00:57:10.760 --> 00:57:14.180
At that time, the basketball club's
older students were cleaning,

00:57:14.180 --> 00:57:17.790
So you couldn't have hid in the gym storage
and gotten stuck there, either.

00:57:17.790 --> 00:57:20.950
The pool is under construction,
so all that's left is the gym.

00:57:21.600 --> 00:57:23.960
That's why I thought that would be
the only place you could have been.

00:57:24.620 --> 00:57:29.460
Besides, you were looking underneath the stairs
a while ago right before the gym class.

00:57:31.950 --> 00:57:33.590
How's that? Are you surprised?

00:57:33.990 --> 00:57:37.890
You're always looking after me, Shinichi.

00:57:39.170 --> 00:57:41.300
You idiot, it's nothing like that.

00:57:41.730 --> 00:57:43.560
Hey, your face is turning red!

00:57:43.850 --> 00:57:46.850
What are you talking about?
It's just because of the sunset.

00:57:54.300 --> 00:57:56.330
All right, I get it.

00:57:56.330 --> 00:58:00.830
The "It's the same as that time" you said yesterday was about this, right?

00:58:01.880 --> 00:58:03.570
Then what you were trying to say earlier was ...

00:58:03.570 --> 00:58:06.350
"We're going to win,"

00:58:06.350 --> 00:58:11.190
"Because the only one who can find me is Shinichi," right?

00:58:11.190 --> 00:58:12.880
It's nothing like that!

00:58:13.130 --> 00:58:16.120
What's this? Your face is a bit red!

00:58:16.120 --> 00:58:18.800
What are you talking about?
That's just the sunset.

00:58:34.100 --> 00:58:36.840
Uncle, what was he doing at Kusaka's?

00:58:38.450 --> 00:58:39.340
Yes?

00:58:41.660 --> 00:58:43.320
Oh, it's the boy this time.

00:58:43.830 --> 00:58:45.160
I came to play.

00:58:48.160 --> 00:58:51.860
I saw this a bit earlier, but this sure is a cool laptop.

00:58:51.860 --> 00:58:54.170
Yeah, it's a commercial product, so ...

00:58:58.610 --> 00:59:00.440
That's not something kids should read.

00:59:00.440 --> 00:59:01.870
Okay.

00:59:03.980 --> 00:59:07.060
Hey, this is the same as the Professor's !

00:59:07.550 --> 00:59:09.560
Huh, I don't hear anything.

00:59:09.950 --> 00:59:11.560
Brat ...

00:59:12.200 --> 00:59:13.390
Get out.

00:59:15.040 --> 00:59:18.200
I suppose no one leaves the evidence behind forever.

00:59:34.430 --> 00:59:37.920
Aww, our trip turned out to be a disaster.

00:59:38.180 --> 00:59:40.610
Don't say things like that, Genta-kun.

00:59:40.610 --> 00:59:42.230
This is a serious case.

00:59:42.230 --> 00:59:43.930
Right ...

00:59:44.150 --> 00:59:48.110
But why do people hurt each other?

00:59:48.110 --> 00:59:50.780
If only everyone could get along.

00:59:50.780 --> 00:59:52.270
That's impossible.

00:59:53.320 --> 00:59:55.270
People have emotions.

00:59:55.900 --> 01:00:00.440
A troublesome attribute that's not only invisible, but also changes easily.

01:00:01.030 --> 01:00:03.620
If it's friendship or love, then that's fine.

01:00:04.230 --> 01:00:07.720
But if by some trigger it changes to malice and vengeance,

01:00:07.720 --> 01:00:10.120
Then that could bring forth thoughts of murder.

01:00:10.400 --> 01:00:15.880
But my Mom and Dad are fighting all the time, but they still get along well.

01:00:16.290 --> 01:00:20.090
That's because they love each other.

01:00:21.390 --> 01:00:28.100
Just as Ai-kun said, a person can easily
become the giver or the receiver of pain.

01:00:28.460 --> 01:00:33.600
In order to keep something like that from happening,
one must always hold good feelings for others.

01:00:33.920 --> 01:00:36.270
Good feelings for others ...

01:00:36.830 --> 01:00:37.980
Professor!

01:00:40.050 --> 01:00:42.740
I want to borrow something from you.

01:00:45.240 --> 01:00:47.950
Nishitama Central Police Station

01:00:55.690 --> 01:00:57.420
The seatbelt's lock.

01:00:59.960 --> 01:01:01.300
Chiba-kun, come here a moment.

01:01:01.580 --> 01:01:02.450
Sure ...

01:01:04.240 --> 01:01:05.580
Did you find something?

01:01:06.080 --> 01:01:06.800
Look at this.

01:01:07.480 --> 01:01:10.140
The seatbelt's lock?

01:01:10.140 --> 01:01:14.690
Do you see this unusual burn mark left behind here?
It's as though something was tied there.

01:01:15.210 --> 01:01:20.230
I see it. It's roughly the width of a kite string.

01:01:22.440 --> 01:01:24.240
A kite string, huh ...

01:01:28.510 --> 01:01:30.440
Huh? What are you doing, Uncle?

01:01:30.440 --> 01:01:34.010
Where have you been all this time?
The party's starting soon.

01:01:35.580 --> 01:01:39.460
Oh, Mouri-san. Chief Inspector Megure wants you to come for a second.

01:01:39.460 --> 01:01:40.630
The Chief Inspector?

01:01:40.980 --> 01:01:42.540
All right.

01:01:42.540 --> 01:01:43.270
Me too!

01:01:43.270 --> 01:01:44.960
You stay behind and get ready.

01:01:49.470 --> 01:01:53.430
I see. So there are suspicions about
Mr. Yashiro Hidetoshi's accident, too.

01:01:53.690 --> 01:02:00.500
Yes. From what Satou-san stated, the kite string mark on the seat belt is suspicious.

01:02:00.500 --> 01:02:03.440
How about it, Mouri-kun?
Can you think of anything?

01:02:04.740 --> 01:02:08.320
Even if you say so ... What were the
other items left behind by the deceased?

01:02:08.560 --> 01:02:12.780
Right. There was a juice can that was burnt to
a crisp and a few miscellaneous items like that,

01:02:12.780 --> 01:02:17.670
But it says here that they've
all been tossed out already.

01:02:17.670 --> 01:02:21.850
Hmm, a juice can and kite string, huh ...

01:02:22.910 --> 01:02:24.420
Maybe if that was used ...

01:02:33.210 --> 01:02:34.350
Were you all surprised?

01:02:34.670 --> 01:02:36.140
You little brat!

01:02:36.430 --> 01:02:40.880
I actually thought of shaking a can of soda and making it go psshhhh,

01:02:40.880 --> 01:02:42.360
But they weren't selling any soda ...

01:02:42.650 --> 01:02:44.150
Soda...!!??

01:02:45.390 --> 01:02:47.890
I thought my heart was going to stop.

01:02:48.900 --> 01:02:51.370
Ahhh! Being surprised by a can could be ...

01:02:51.740 --> 01:02:53.040
A stun grenade.

01:02:55.070 --> 01:02:58.120
Perhaps the culprit used a stun grenade.

01:02:58.640 --> 01:02:59.880
That's right.

01:03:00.200 --> 01:03:03.350
What's this, Shiratori-kun? A stun...?

01:03:03.350 --> 01:03:05.840
Stun grenade. Also known as a flash bomb.

01:03:06.440 --> 01:03:10.350
With a bright flash and an explosion,
it stuns the opponent's movement.

01:03:10.350 --> 01:03:13.850
It's a type of grenade shaped like a juice can.

01:03:14.210 --> 01:03:19.060
For instance, tying a kite string to the stun
grenade which has its pin pulled out already,

01:03:19.060 --> 01:03:23.110
And then tying the other end of the kite string to the seat belt's lock,

01:03:23.550 --> 01:03:26.930
Just as one pulls on the lock to secure his seat belt ...

01:03:30.420 --> 01:03:36.540
I see. Even if he didn't have a heart attack,
he would be unable to drive after he lost consciousness,

01:03:36.540 --> 01:03:39.500
And the car would run straight off the cliff.

01:03:43.110 --> 01:03:46.650
But a stun grenade isn't something so easily ...

01:03:46.650 --> 01:03:51.010
Then again, we're in an era
where a person can get anything.

01:03:51.330 --> 01:03:58.480
Yes, and if he only wanted to shock the victim,
then he didn't even need to use a real one.

01:03:58.710 --> 01:04:02.230
Even a large cracker could have done the trick.

01:04:06.300 --> 01:04:09.200
Chief Inspector, we've just received a call.

01:04:10.280 --> 01:04:12.990
They say that they found a body
that's believed to be President Yashiro.

01:04:15.950 --> 01:04:18.820
Captain, I have something that
 I wish to talk to you about.

01:04:18.820 --> 01:04:19.660
What is it?

01:04:19.890 --> 01:04:24.170
It's about the welcome party at 5:00 P.M.,
I want you to cancel it.

01:04:24.760 --> 01:04:28.500
If the culprit is planning his next murder,

01:04:28.500 --> 01:04:31.380
Then there's a good chance that he'll
try to use the confusion of the party.

01:04:31.730 --> 01:04:33.390
But ...

01:04:33.820 --> 01:04:35.580
Please, Captain.

01:04:35.580 --> 01:04:37.410
No, Chief Inspector.

01:04:38.690 --> 01:04:40.600
Let's have this party.

01:04:41.670 --> 01:04:44.640
All the questions should be answered there.

01:04:44.640 --> 01:04:46.680
Mouri-kun, did you ...

01:04:46.680 --> 01:04:48.860
Did it come, the usual thing?!

01:04:51.410 --> 01:04:53.030
But he's not asleep.

01:04:57.350 --> 01:04:59.540
Are you sure, Uncle?

01:05:18.840 --> 01:05:20.820
All right. I'm gonna party!

01:05:20.820 --> 01:05:23.020
I'll make up for the half day I spent resting.

01:05:23.190 --> 01:05:25.110
Sonoko ...

01:05:27.110 --> 01:05:28.890
Hey, why don't you ask Ran-oneesan?

01:05:28.890 --> 01:05:30.460
About the you-know-what.

01:05:30.460 --> 01:05:31.820
I suppose.

01:05:32.900 --> 01:05:35.530
A gold medal made from sea shells?

01:05:35.870 --> 01:05:39.220
Although the string became too short
and it turned into a bracelet ...

01:05:39.220 --> 01:05:41.570
So you didn't notice it after all.

01:05:41.570 --> 01:05:42.500
What a pity.

01:05:42.750 --> 01:05:45.420
I'm so sorry. I promise I'll look at it later.

01:05:45.860 --> 01:05:49.920
But thanks, guys. I appreciate your thoughtfulness.

01:05:54.010 --> 01:05:57.140
Everyone, welcome to the St. Aphrodite.

01:05:57.710 --> 01:06:03.850
I will be your host for tonight, Tsujimoto Natsuho.

01:06:05.380 --> 01:06:06.690
Thank you.

01:06:07.310 --> 01:06:11.150
First, let me introduce to you our main staff.

01:06:11.150 --> 01:06:14.010
First, our chief purser, Misaki Naoya.

01:06:17.030 --> 01:06:20.040
Next is the doctor on board, Doctor Mizu Tsubu.

01:06:23.070 --> 01:06:25.800
Our head chef, Chef Shiomi Katsuhiko.

01:06:27.710 --> 01:06:29.680
Did you find out who the culprit is?

01:06:29.680 --> 01:06:34.620
Yeah. But I still can't find any solid evidence.

01:06:35.640 --> 01:06:37.620
Now then, I've kept you all waiting.

01:06:37.620 --> 01:06:40.220
Our captain, Kaidou Wataru.

01:06:45.740 --> 01:06:50.690
Before I say my greetings, I would like to introduce you
 to the beautiful woman who designed this ship.

01:06:51.350 --> 01:06:54.110
The designer, Akioshi Minako-san.

01:07:03.230 --> 01:07:07.250
Captain, is it true that Chief Takae was murdered?

01:07:07.530 --> 01:07:10.630
There's a rumor that President Yashiro is also missing.

01:07:11.010 --> 01:07:11.920
That's ...

01:07:12.400 --> 01:07:15.490
You're the inspector, right?
Did you catch the culprit yet?

01:07:15.490 --> 01:07:18.490
Are you sure it's safe for us to participate in this party?

01:07:20.770 --> 01:07:23.430
Calm down. Everyone, please calm down.

01:07:23.820 --> 01:07:25.600
What in the word is going on?

01:07:25.600 --> 01:07:29.050
Well ... Mouri-san?

01:07:29.050 --> 01:07:31.480
Huh, Mouri-san?!

01:07:31.480 --> 01:07:34.190
Everyone, please calm yourselves.

01:07:34.830 --> 01:07:36.870
There's no need to worry.

01:07:36.870 --> 01:07:44.200
The gruesome serial killer has already been identified by me, Mouri Kogorou!

01:07:44.810 --> 01:07:46.620
We've been waiting, great detective!

01:07:48.800 --> 01:07:54.570
The culprit who murdered Chief Yashiro Takae, and President Entarou.

01:07:55.050 --> 01:07:59.800
That is ... Akiyoshi Minako-san, you!

01:08:03.470 --> 01:08:09.970
Her motive was revenge for Yashiro Hideto-shi's accident which occurred about half a month ago.

01:08:10.360 --> 01:08:15.940
That accident was actually a murder case orchestrated by the Yashiro family.

01:08:16.230 --> 01:08:20.400
But why would Akiyoshi-san take revenge upon Yashiro-san's death?

01:08:20.860 --> 01:08:25.370
That is most likely because Minako-san and
Hideto-shi had a romantic relationship.

01:08:25.730 --> 01:08:27.930
Hold on, Mouri-san.

01:08:28.300 --> 01:08:32.700
It's true that I did admire Yashiro-sensei
 as an important superior.

01:08:33.050 --> 01:08:35.130
But I didn't have any feelings for him.

01:08:35.460 --> 01:08:41.010
Also, I was talking to Kusaka-san over the phone
in my room during the time of the crime as an alibi.

01:08:41.180 --> 01:08:50.520
But in reality, you let Kusaka-san read the story on his own for about 20 minutes,

01:08:51.010 --> 01:08:54.270
That means there's no alibi
for you during those 20 minutes.

01:08:54.270 --> 01:08:55.940
Enough already.

01:08:56.330 --> 01:09:00.320
If Kusaka-san stopped reading in the middle and asked me something,

01:09:00.320 --> 01:09:03.320
He would know that there wasn't anyone on the other end of the phone.

01:09:03.320 --> 01:09:06.990
I'm not stupid enough to try
to create such an idiotic alibi.

01:09:07.380 --> 01:09:11.580
If you still insist on saying that I'm the culprit,
then show me the evidence right now!

01:09:13.260 --> 01:09:16.210
Hey! You have proof, right, Mouri-kun?

01:09:16.790 --> 01:09:19.090
Well ...

01:09:19.370 --> 01:09:24.090
Could Dad ... Could he suspect Minako-san just because she looks like Mom?

01:09:24.610 --> 01:09:26.130
Well, Mouri-san?

01:09:26.130 --> 01:09:28.890
Sorry. I need a little washroom break ...

01:09:28.890 --> 01:09:30.390
A break?

01:09:38.720 --> 01:09:40.280
I found it.

01:09:40.640 --> 01:09:44.440
Chief Inspector, we should do something while everyone's still laughing.

01:09:44.440 --> 01:09:46.140
But ...

01:09:46.140 --> 01:09:48.280
No need to worry, Chief Inspector Megure.

01:09:48.670 --> 01:09:51.010
I know the true culprit.

01:09:51.010 --> 01:09:53.450
Really, Professor Agasa?

01:09:54.700 --> 01:09:57.000
This time, it's the Professor's deduction show!

01:09:57.270 --> 01:10:01.620
Everyone, do you know the
original meaning of a cruise?

01:10:01.620 --> 01:10:03.710
It's an act of piracy.

01:10:03.710 --> 01:10:07.970
Apparently the name came from pirates
searching for prey and zigzagging on their voyage.

01:10:08.780 --> 01:10:11.820
There is a pirate on this ship as well.

01:10:12.270 --> 01:10:17.980
A pirate who steals others' lives instead of their wealth. A pirate by the name of murderer.

01:10:18.450 --> 01:10:25.030
Yes. That pirate is ...
The script writer, Kusaka Hironari-san, you!

01:10:25.500 --> 01:10:30.100
You sure say strange things.
Weren't you listening to Minako-san's words?

01:10:30.100 --> 01:10:35.510
During the time of the incident,
I was telling her about my story on the phone.

01:10:35.510 --> 01:10:37.580
You mean this story?

01:10:39.020 --> 01:10:41.590
Okazaki Nanami loved the ocean ...

01:10:42.000 --> 01:10:45.350
ever since she was born.

01:10:45.350 --> 01:10:48.550
She loved its vastness more than anything else.

01:10:48.670 --> 01:10:50.920
It's a simple trick.

01:10:50.920 --> 01:10:56.000
You used a tape recording you premade, left it by the phone,

01:10:56.000 --> 01:10:58.520
And murdered the two during that time.

01:10:58.520 --> 01:11:01.150
That can't be. I know I erased that already!

01:11:01.150 --> 01:11:02.420
Erased?

01:11:02.420 --> 01:11:06.770
No, you thought you erased it.

01:11:07.170 --> 01:11:12.120
Something important such as this, if you don't confirm it properly, then it could be life-threatening.

01:11:14.790 --> 01:11:16.720
Forged evidence, right?

01:11:16.720 --> 01:11:20.520
That tape ... You used his voice and recreated it, right?

01:11:20.520 --> 01:11:22.670
Yeah, more or less.

01:11:22.670 --> 01:11:26.550
But there's still further solid proof.

01:11:26.900 --> 01:11:31.550
But that can't be used as 
evidence for the murder, can it?

01:11:31.830 --> 01:11:33.520
The evidence is right there.

01:11:33.520 --> 01:11:34.640
Look there

01:11:36.230 --> 01:11:38.560
What's wrong, Onii-san?

01:11:38.940 --> 01:11:42.180
There's a blackish hair mixed with your red ones.

01:11:43.710 --> 01:11:46.190
Isn't that ... Blood?

01:11:46.190 --> 01:11:47.440
Blood?

01:11:48.780 --> 01:11:50.780
Kusaka-san ...

01:11:50.780 --> 01:11:52.160
I get it.

01:11:52.160 --> 01:11:55.040
Oniisan, after you did those bad things,
you looked into the mirror,

01:11:55.040 --> 01:11:59.500
But since your hair color is very
similar to blood, you didn't notice it.

01:12:00.130 --> 01:12:01.960
But your should remember this.

01:12:02.490 --> 01:12:05.100
Blood will clot as time goes on,

01:12:05.100 --> 01:12:06.920
And the color will change.

01:12:08.670 --> 01:12:12.600
Also, could you remove that scarf around your neck?

01:12:13.120 --> 01:12:17.200
If my deduction is right,
there still should be marks left over.

01:12:17.770 --> 01:12:23.810
From President Yashiro's nail or finger marks
when he fought back so hard against your attack.

01:12:24.150 --> 01:12:25.690
Excuse me.

01:12:28.490 --> 01:12:33.120
Kusaka-san, may we hear your
 story in detail in another room?

01:12:33.320 --> 01:12:35.960
Hold on. Geez.

01:12:35.960 --> 01:12:37.240
I still have ...

01:12:38.030 --> 01:12:40.040
One last trick up my sleeve!

01:12:43.700 --> 01:12:46.700
Don't move! If you do, I'll detonate the bombs!

01:12:46.700 --> 01:12:47.710
Bombs!

01:12:48.880 --> 01:12:51.880
If you don't want me to sink this ship,
then listen to what I say!

01:12:59.910 --> 01:13:02.640
That's the guy who attacked me!

01:13:03.790 --> 01:13:05.150
You finally remembered?

01:13:05.790 --> 01:13:09.070
Please calm down.
Why are you doing this?

01:13:09.070 --> 01:13:10.500
I'm taking revenge for my father.

01:13:10.500 --> 01:13:11.360
Revenge?

01:13:11.570 --> 01:13:18.080
15 years ago, the crew member who
died on the St. Yashiro was my father!

01:13:19.660 --> 01:13:22.290
I see, that was...!

01:13:22.610 --> 01:13:26.820
Two years ago, I heard a strange rumor from one of my father's friends,

01:13:26.820 --> 01:13:30.260
who came to visit my father's grave, about the incident.

01:13:31.930 --> 01:13:36.850
During the time, Yashiro Cruise's Chief and First-mate Executive Entarou and Takae,

01:13:36.850 --> 01:13:40.830
Decided to sink the ship for its insurance.

01:13:41.480 --> 01:13:47.500
Furthermore, there was a crew who was after the accomplishments of Captain Okita and his seat,

01:13:47.500 --> 01:13:50.440
They brought in their first man, Kaidou First Mate.

01:13:54.410 --> 01:13:55.990
You, who got talked into it,

01:13:56.220 --> 01:13:59.510
put Captain Okita to sleep with drugged coffee.

01:13:59.510 --> 01:14:02.180
Purposefully crashing the ship to the iceberg.

01:14:05.420 --> 01:14:09.530
And at the same time, you blew up the bombs you'd set up beforehand.

01:14:12.180 --> 01:14:17.590
The locations to put the bombs were most likely organized by the designer Yashiro Hideto-shi.

01:14:18.060 --> 01:14:19.550
Are you saying that Sensei...?

01:14:20.020 --> 01:14:23.020
How did you kill President Yashiro?

01:14:23.270 --> 01:14:26.720
He lunged at me and choked me on the floor,

01:14:26.720 --> 01:14:30.460
so I threw him into the ocean as the ship swayed.

01:14:30.460 --> 01:14:33.990
And, just as you did, I was planning to blow up this ship,

01:14:34.400 --> 01:14:37.790
And kill you in the confusion.

01:14:38.460 --> 01:14:39.700
What a bunch of nonsense.

01:14:40.150 --> 01:14:43.790
Just a minute! At least remove your finger from that remote button.

01:14:44.160 --> 01:14:46.120
Shut up! Don't come any closer!

01:14:54.670 --> 01:14:55.340
He's gone!

01:14:57.760 --> 01:14:58.950
You're not getting away!

01:14:59.640 --> 01:15:00.740
Conan-kun!

01:15:01.100 --> 01:15:02.240
Get him!

01:15:24.200 --> 01:15:25.280
Damn it.

01:15:27.520 --> 01:15:29.090
Wait, Conan-kun!

01:15:29.090 --> 01:15:29.880
Wait up.

01:15:30.700 --> 01:15:31.790
Hey, you guys ...

01:15:31.790 --> 01:15:33.290
We're going, too.

01:15:33.290 --> 01:15:35.860
We're not letting you take all the credit.

01:15:35.860 --> 01:15:37.050
Hey, Haibara ...

01:15:37.650 --> 01:15:39.380
Well, like they said ...

01:15:42.410 --> 01:15:43.890
Don't get shaken off.

01:16:35.210 --> 01:16:36.720
Shift to the left!

01:16:45.160 --> 01:16:46.520
Now right!

01:16:52.060 --> 01:16:53.250
We passed him!

01:16:55.300 --> 01:16:56.890
Haibara, take the wheel.

01:17:22.300 --> 01:17:23.990
Conan-kun!

01:17:24.230 --> 01:17:25.990
You did it, Conan!

01:17:28.270 --> 01:17:30.060
All right!

01:17:30.060 --> 01:17:33.840
The Detective Boys win again!

01:17:39.370 --> 01:17:40.920
Hey!

01:17:40.920 --> 01:17:43.220
Are you all okay?

01:17:43.220 --> 01:17:44.820
Hey!

01:17:46.470 --> 01:17:48.010
Don't you guys ever do that again!

01:17:48.590 --> 01:17:51.020
He was a suspect for a murder case!

01:17:51.450 --> 01:17:54.070
What if something went wrong?

01:17:54.070 --> 01:17:55.520
We're sorry ...

01:18:06.760 --> 01:18:08.680
Chief Inspector Megure ...

01:18:08.680 --> 01:18:11.580
H-How many bombs did he set up?

01:18:24.650 --> 01:18:25.970
How is it, Izawa-kun?

01:18:26.310 --> 01:18:30.800
Captain, a number of holes were opened by the bombs.

01:18:30.800 --> 01:18:31.770
What about the chamber locks?

01:18:32.230 --> 01:18:36.120
We locked them, but the water is
reaching from the 3rd block to the 4th.

01:18:36.420 --> 01:18:37.270
What?!

01:18:37.820 --> 01:18:39.770
Captain, please give the order for evacuation.

01:18:41.760 --> 01:18:42.780
Captain!

01:18:44.760 --> 01:18:46.780
Evacuate all personnel.

01:18:49.670 --> 01:18:52.790
All guests, this is your voyage guide, Norizama.

01:18:53.120 --> 01:18:58.260
Please take your emergency life vests
and move to the deck on the first floor.

01:18:58.260 --> 01:19:02.630
This is not a drill. I repeat, this is not a drill!

01:19:03.190 --> 01:19:04.800
Please move calmly.

01:19:05.080 --> 01:19:08.900
All crew members are to guide all guests to the designated locations.

01:19:13.010 --> 01:19:16.680
It's not here. The gold medal that
those kids were talking about.

01:19:16.680 --> 01:19:18.020
Where did it go?

01:19:18.220 --> 01:19:19.040
Ran ...

01:19:19.470 --> 01:19:21.360
Hey, we're leaving. Hurry up!

01:19:21.360 --> 01:19:22.540
Ran, let's go.

01:19:33.430 --> 01:19:37.110
There's no need to rush, there's still plenty of time.

01:19:37.110 --> 01:19:39.330
Please continue moving without pushing.

01:19:39.330 --> 01:19:41.580
Dad, where's Conan-kun and everyone else?

01:19:41.580 --> 01:19:43.130
They're fine.

01:19:43.520 --> 01:19:45.770
According to Chief Inspector Megure,

01:19:45.770 --> 01:19:51.940
After they went chasing Kusaka in a motor boat,
they were picked up by a nearby cruiser.

01:19:51.940 --> 01:19:53.140
That's good.

01:19:58.950 --> 01:20:02.900
Ran, you two leave on this boat.

01:20:03.580 --> 01:20:05.400
I'll go on a different one.

01:20:05.400 --> 01:20:06.130
But ...

01:20:06.130 --> 01:20:07.370
Well then, see you later.

01:20:07.370 --> 01:20:08.320
Dad!

01:20:08.700 --> 01:20:11.480
Don't rush. Follow the person in front of you.

01:20:11.480 --> 01:20:14.400
Once you hit the water, get away from the ship as quickly as possible.

01:20:14.400 --> 01:20:17.950
If you get sucked down by the ship's whirlpool,
there won't be anything left of you.

01:20:17.950 --> 01:20:18.760
Understood.

01:20:19.540 --> 01:20:22.160
It's blazing in here.

01:20:22.160 --> 01:20:24.710
We're in a crisis, suck it up.

01:20:25.050 --> 01:20:28.420
But when it's hot, it's hot!

01:20:29.460 --> 01:20:30.300
I remembered now!

01:20:30.300 --> 01:20:31.770
What?

01:20:31.770 --> 01:20:33.790
I dropped it where I hid for hide and seek.

01:20:33.790 --> 01:20:34.800
You mean the gold medal?

01:20:35.390 --> 01:20:37.890
I'm lowering the raft. Hold on tightly.

01:20:37.890 --> 01:20:39.680
Wait, I'm getting off.

01:20:40.010 --> 01:20:41.080
Hey Ran!

01:20:41.080 --> 01:20:42.760
I'm going to go and get it so go on ahead.

01:20:42.760 --> 01:20:43.310
But ...

01:20:43.870 --> 01:20:46.760
It's true that it's just a medal made from sea shells.

01:20:46.760 --> 01:20:49.320
But to me, it's a precious treasure.

01:20:49.550 --> 01:20:50.700
Well, I'll catch you later.

01:20:50.700 --> 01:20:51.820
Wait a second, Ran!

01:21:08.310 --> 01:21:10.050
This is it!

01:21:21.350 --> 01:21:23.730
We sure were lucky,

01:21:23.730 --> 01:21:26.300
that this ship was nearby.

01:21:26.300 --> 01:21:29.230
I wonder if the people on the ship are okay?

01:21:29.230 --> 01:21:31.000
I'm worried.

01:21:34.370 --> 01:21:37.770
Don't worry, she's probably on the emergency boat and ...

01:21:37.770 --> 01:21:43.250
Kusaka said that he was planning to kill Kaidou-san in the confusion.

01:21:43.660 --> 01:21:47.460
But aren't there a bit too many bombs for that?

01:21:47.460 --> 01:21:51.460
It's as though he really was trying to sink the ship.

01:21:51.460 --> 01:21:54.680
And that trick he used for his alibi,

01:21:54.680 --> 01:21:56.470
now that I think about it, it's a bit too simple.

01:21:56.850 --> 01:22:00.000
If Minako-san said anything
in the middle of the conversation,

01:22:00.000 --> 01:22:01.470
then the trick would fall apart right there.

01:22:01.890 --> 01:22:04.180
Maybe he tested it a few times already.

01:22:04.180 --> 01:22:08.100
He probably thought he could use it to create his alibi,

01:22:08.100 --> 01:22:10.500
after he confirmed the fact that she wouldn't interrupt.

01:22:10.500 --> 01:22:11.710
She did say ...

01:22:12.120 --> 01:22:15.240
If I say something in the middle, he gets angry.

01:22:16.490 --> 01:22:17.320
Chief Inspector Megure.

01:22:18.370 --> 01:22:21.540
I just had a talk with the coast guards.

01:22:21.540 --> 01:22:25.940
Apparently, they discovered a fruit knife
stabbed into President Yashiro's back.

01:22:25.940 --> 01:22:26.750
What?

01:22:27.420 --> 01:22:29.160
What does this mean?

01:22:29.160 --> 01:22:32.270
Kusaka didn't say anything about a knife.

01:22:35.090 --> 01:22:36.970
It was 10:11 A.M.

01:22:37.200 --> 01:22:39.460
It was about 10:15 A.M.

01:22:39.460 --> 01:22:41.850
No, it wasn't Kusaka ...

01:22:42.280 --> 01:22:43.840
Then who ...

01:22:43.840 --> 01:22:46.380
They really don't look like they're in their 50's.

01:22:54.770 --> 01:22:55.950
Hey, Conan ...

01:22:55.950 --> 01:22:57.860
Where are you going Conan-kun?

01:22:57.860 --> 01:22:59.070
Conan-kun.

01:23:01.430 --> 01:23:03.080
I wonder what it is.

01:23:03.670 --> 01:23:05.940
Something just doesn't feel right.

01:23:05.940 --> 01:23:11.090
A feeling that says if I just let it sink like this, I'd be losing something that I'll never be able to get back.

01:23:11.090 --> 01:23:13.460
You mean about the case?

01:23:13.830 --> 01:23:15.460
Yeah, probably.

01:23:16.270 --> 01:23:17.180
Most likely.

01:23:20.870 --> 01:23:22.120
Conan-kun ...

01:23:25.040 --> 01:23:30.420
The case? Are you sure that's all, Kudou-kun?

01:23:36.680 --> 01:23:39.630
If my deduction is right, then the real culprit is ...

01:23:45.410 --> 01:23:46.440
Captain.

01:23:48.540 --> 01:23:50.830
The evacuation of the guests is now complete.

01:23:52.200 --> 01:23:54.380
I'll take the life raft.

01:23:54.380 --> 01:23:57.050
You go ahead on the emergency boat first
once you've gathered all the crew members.

01:23:57.050 --> 01:23:58.080
Understood.

01:24:07.360 --> 01:24:11.930
Aren't you going down with the ship, Captain?

01:24:14.710 --> 01:24:18.120
You! What are you still doing here?
Hurry and evacuate!

01:24:18.120 --> 01:24:20.420
You should have some recollection of this.

01:24:21.050 --> 01:24:23.950
It was something my father loved.

01:24:24.440 --> 01:24:26.140
An origami boat ...

01:24:27.870 --> 01:24:29.080
Are you ...

01:24:29.600 --> 01:24:32.780
That's right. I'm the daughter of Captain Okita,

01:24:32.780 --> 01:24:36.630
the one you and the Yashiro family murdered.

01:24:38.360 --> 01:24:42.140
Sorry to tell you this, but I've
destroyed the remaining life rafts.

01:24:42.360 --> 01:24:43.730
H-how could you?

01:24:43.730 --> 01:24:45.140
Don't move!

01:24:45.900 --> 01:24:47.850
This is a pretty small place.

01:24:48.610 --> 01:24:53.690
Let's go somewhere bigger and have a long chat about this as we feel the salty air.

01:25:15.610 --> 01:25:17.630
It was half a year ago,

01:25:18.310 --> 01:25:22.130
That Kusaka came to see me,
saying it was for his drama research.

01:25:22.610 --> 01:25:29.140
But I found it strange that he held more interest in the Yashiro family, which had nothing to do with his research.

01:25:29.920 --> 01:25:33.130
That was when I took the chance when he left to go to the washroom ...

01:25:41.110 --> 01:25:44.910
I saw, "The truth behind the St. Yashiro Number 1 Sinking Case".

01:25:46.220 --> 01:25:49.080
And learned that was Kusaka's true goal.

01:25:50.940 --> 01:25:52.780
I didn't think it could be true,

01:25:52.780 --> 01:25:55.250
But I asked Yashiro Hideto the following day.

01:25:56.350 --> 01:25:59.960
Once I gave him a bit of high-proof alcohol, he spilled everything.

01:26:00.900 --> 01:26:06.160
The truth about how that sinking case was not an accident, but a planned murder.

01:26:07.590 --> 01:26:10.820
Without even knowing that I was Okita's daughter.

01:26:13.810 --> 01:26:17.150
I-I didn't know. I was ordered by the Chief, and ...

01:26:17.150 --> 01:26:18.560
I don't need excuses!

01:26:19.190 --> 01:26:22.440
I'll have you chase after the Yashiro family.

01:26:22.870 --> 01:26:27.450
For my father who died a depressing death.

01:26:29.510 --> 01:26:31.670
Damn it! Let me get there in time!

01:26:32.920 --> 01:26:34.830
Please, forgive me!

01:26:35.550 --> 01:26:37.820
Goodbye, Captain.

01:26:44.880 --> 01:26:46.040
Hold it!

01:26:50.790 --> 01:26:55.440
So you were the real culprit, Akiyoshi Minako-san.

01:26:55.860 --> 01:26:56.690
Uncle...!

01:26:57.210 --> 01:26:58.150
Don't move!

01:27:01.250 --> 01:27:04.350
Sorry, but I made sure that gun
couldn't be used anymore.

01:27:07.130 --> 01:27:10.830
I found it in your room during my washroom break.

01:27:15.660 --> 01:27:16.290
Captain.

01:27:19.510 --> 01:27:23.420
I'll have a long talk with you later.

01:27:26.390 --> 01:27:29.020
Akiyoshi-san, based on my deductions ...

01:27:29.020 --> 01:27:32.890
Let's just drop the act.
All three of us are going to die anyways.

01:27:33.100 --> 01:27:37.890
A deduction like that on top
of a sinking ship is pointless.

01:27:39.150 --> 01:27:40.900
How can I stop?

01:27:41.660 --> 01:27:45.360
Revealing the truth is what detectives live for.

01:27:47.390 --> 01:27:53.760
Most likely, you learned that Kusaka was planning to murder the four of them.

01:27:54.310 --> 01:27:57.000
But there was an impossibility in his plan.

01:27:57.590 --> 01:28:03.500
That's why you killed Hideto-shi first as though
he died from an accident caused by a heart attack.

01:28:04.450 --> 01:28:07.000
Using a self-made stun grenade.

01:28:09.220 --> 01:28:14.160
With Hideto-shi's death, Kusaka changed the four murders to just three.

01:28:14.160 --> 01:28:17.230
And decided to use you as an alibi.

01:28:17.510 --> 01:28:24.230
Knowing that, you decided to take revenge with your own hands by using his plan.

01:28:24.540 --> 01:28:28.450
First, you set up bombs separately from Kusaka's.

01:28:28.870 --> 01:28:30.950
This is the ship you designed.

01:28:30.950 --> 01:28:34.880
You should know exactly where to hit for it to sink.

01:28:35.240 --> 01:28:39.290
Then, this morning at 10:00 A.M., you received the phone call from Kusaka,

01:28:39.290 --> 01:28:42.700
and dashed out of your room
just as Kusaka began to read his story.

01:28:42.700 --> 01:28:45.730
You knocked out Chief Takae who was taking a bath,

01:28:45.730 --> 01:28:49.260
and put on the bath robe and pretended to be the Chief.

01:28:49.770 --> 01:28:56.680
Then Kusaka came in and thought you were
Chief Takae since you were wearing a bathrobe,

01:28:57.790 --> 01:29:01.110
And you pretended to fight him by trying to take the knife from him,

01:29:01.110 --> 01:29:04.770
and stabbed it into your own stomach where you'd already put a blood-like substance.

01:29:05.040 --> 01:29:09.140
And after Kusaka left, thinking he
had done what he came for,

01:29:09.140 --> 01:29:11.280
you murdered Chief Takae.

01:29:13.560 --> 01:29:18.550
After you wiped the reddish substance from the floor and put on the windbreaker, you left the room.

01:29:33.720 --> 01:29:39.680
At the time, I thought it was because you didn't want me to see your face that you turned your back to me.

01:29:40.260 --> 01:29:42.460
But I realized it later.

01:29:42.900 --> 01:29:44.690
Perhaps it was a woman.

01:29:44.950 --> 01:29:48.150
Instinctively trying to turn away her chest.

01:29:48.320 --> 01:29:49.330
I see ...

01:29:53.200 --> 01:29:54.960
That's why that time, he ...

01:29:58.200 --> 01:30:01.370
Afterwards, you went to the basement marina.

01:30:01.770 --> 01:30:07.040
When you got there, it was just when the
President sat on top of Kusaka, choking him.

01:30:07.850 --> 01:30:12.050
You quickly ran up to the two of them,
then held both feet of the President ...

01:30:12.710 --> 01:30:13.470
Both feet...?

01:30:14.430 --> 01:30:20.260
That's right. You made sure that you didn't touch either of Kusaka's feet,

01:30:21.230 --> 01:30:24.440
Right, right ... Stabbed him in the back.

01:30:31.420 --> 01:30:37.280
Since you hid yourself right afterwards,
Kusaka believed he did it himself.

01:30:37.280 --> 01:30:40.160
All according to your plan.

01:30:41.510 --> 01:30:44.820
You're indeed the great detective, Mouri Kogorou-san.

01:30:45.360 --> 01:30:51.270
I decided to use that man, because I learned that you were coming on this cruise.

01:30:51.270 --> 01:30:56.380
In order to fool the eyes of the great detective, I needed a fake culprit.

01:30:56.730 --> 01:31:00.890
Furthermore, I needed a culprit who really did think he had done it.

01:31:01.620 --> 01:31:09.270
That man called my father, whose fate went down with the ship, the representation of an anachronism on his laptop.

01:31:09.990 --> 01:31:12.740
I won't forgive anyone who talks badly about my father.

01:31:13.180 --> 01:31:15.750
You're the one who cannot be forgiven.

01:31:16.860 --> 01:31:20.050
Not only did you take the lives of those three,

01:31:20.050 --> 01:31:23.290
You put a lot of innocent people in danger,

01:31:23.290 --> 01:31:26.370
And you even sunk the ship
you created to do such an act ...

01:31:27.080 --> 01:31:29.680
I've done detailed simulations over and over again.

01:31:29.680 --> 01:31:34.020
The number of bombs, the amount of water entering the ship, the time it takes for the evacuation,

01:31:34.500 --> 01:31:38.380
And even to the point where I saw that man over there,

01:31:38.380 --> 01:31:43.720
Dying a gruesome, lonely, and depressing death upon these giant blue waves.

01:31:46.520 --> 01:31:51.080
St. Aphrodite was born from nothing.

01:31:51.540 --> 01:31:53.400
Its fate is to return to nothing.

01:31:55.190 --> 01:31:59.410
But since you've managed to figure things out up until this point, I guess I have no choice.

01:31:59.410 --> 01:32:01.280
I'll turn myself in quietly.

01:32:08.170 --> 01:32:11.290
It's not my hobby to fight with a woman.

01:32:12.420 --> 01:32:14.210
Isn't that sexist?

01:32:21.240 --> 01:32:22.350
Uncle ...

01:32:29.180 --> 01:32:32.350
What? Still can't change your hobby?

01:32:33.190 --> 01:32:36.230
Like I said, fighting a woman isn't my hobby.

01:32:36.570 --> 01:32:39.870
All three of us are going to die here anyway.

01:32:39.870 --> 01:32:43.120
That's because you got in the way of my revenge!

01:33:06.890 --> 01:33:08.280
That kid ...

01:33:08.280 --> 01:33:09.200
Shinichi?

01:33:09.200 --> 01:33:09.930
Huh?

01:33:09.930 --> 01:33:11.300
No, nothing ...

01:33:41.920 --> 01:33:44.430
Shall we end this soon ...

01:33:46.110 --> 01:33:47.640
Mouri Kogorou-san?

01:33:58.510 --> 01:34:03.240
I don't really want to see the great detective looking like this, but ...

01:34:03.970 --> 01:34:05.740
Mind your own business.

01:34:22.660 --> 01:34:23.370
Uncle!

01:34:41.480 --> 01:34:43.690
How unlucky,

01:34:44.070 --> 01:34:47.700
to have the great detective
suspect me from the very start.

01:34:48.740 --> 01:34:53.200
Do I look that much like some woman you hate?

01:34:53.490 --> 01:34:55.510
It's just the opposite.

01:34:55.510 --> 01:34:57.850
You resemble her too much.

01:34:58.270 --> 01:35:01.060
So I thought, as long as the culprit wasn't you, then it would be fine.

01:35:01.060 --> 01:35:04.150
As I tried to find evidence to prove your innocence,

01:35:04.150 --> 01:35:05.740
it turned out like this ...

01:35:07.550 --> 01:35:09.040
Uncle!

01:35:09.600 --> 01:35:11.600
Are you all right, Uncle?

01:35:12.020 --> 01:35:14.600
That was a great deduction, Uncle!

01:35:15.250 --> 01:35:17.310
What the heck are you doing here?

01:35:17.680 --> 01:35:19.770
First thing first, we have to get out of here.

01:35:20.580 --> 01:35:21.520
Run away...?

01:35:21.850 --> 01:35:28.100
We can't. All the emergency boats are gone and this woman's destroyed all the life rafts.

01:35:28.100 --> 01:35:29.160
Hey, hey ...

01:35:29.160 --> 01:35:30.660
Captain!

01:35:30.890 --> 01:35:32.310
Captain!

01:35:34.840 --> 01:35:36.040
Captain ...

01:35:36.510 --> 01:35:37.900
We're saved.

01:35:41.530 --> 01:35:43.530
What's this feeling?

01:35:43.930 --> 01:35:46.050
The case has already been solved.

01:35:46.060 --> 01:35:51.310
So what's this stomach turning, unsettling feeling?

01:35:55.280 --> 01:35:57.480
It's going to sink soon. Hurry.

01:36:01.210 --> 01:36:03.830
Hey, you're next. Move it!

01:36:08.280 --> 01:36:10.730
What are you doing? Hurry up and get on!

01:36:12.090 --> 01:36:15.040
W-Where's Ran-neechan?

01:36:15.980 --> 01:36:17.910
Ran got on an emergency boat a long time ago ...

01:36:18.090 --> 01:36:20.620
What? You aren't with Ran?

01:36:21.240 --> 01:36:22.840
Hey, what are you saying?

01:36:23.180 --> 01:36:26.400
She went back to her hiding spot from
playing hide and seek to get her gold medal.

01:36:26.400 --> 01:36:28.840
So I thought she was with you ...

01:36:28.840 --> 01:36:30.300
That's it!

01:36:30.570 --> 01:36:32.420
Hey, hold on a minute!

01:36:50.690 --> 01:36:53.740
Hey, where's Ran?

01:36:57.830 --> 01:36:59.580
Someone!

01:36:59.580 --> 01:37:02.080
Is anyone there?!

01:37:07.850 --> 01:37:13.430
toki ga nagaretemo
Even though seasons may pass,

01:37:09.400 --> 01:37:12.700
Hey, Ran. So you were here all along.

01:37:13.920 --> 01:37:18.430
Shinichi, you'll find me, right?

01:37:14.300 --> 01:37:19.800
bokuno Kokorode
But in my heart,

01:37:18.790 --> 01:37:20.180
Shinichi?

01:37:20.690 --> 01:37:32.940
nannimo kawaranai mabushii mama
It will still be shining as though nothing had changed.

01:37:21.770 --> 01:37:23.850
Hey, where's Ran?

01:37:23.850 --> 01:37:27.360
Ran-neechan knew that I was kicking
 the ball here the entire time.

01:37:27.710 --> 01:37:29.150
That means ...

01:37:31.110 --> 01:37:32.570
the upper deck!

01:37:33.560 --> 01:37:39.740
kaeritakute Kaerenakute
Knowing I can't go back no matter how much I wish to,

01:37:35.720 --> 01:37:37.260
I'll find you.

01:37:37.260 --> 01:37:40.450
I promise I'll find you.
So wait for me, Ran!

01:37:39.750 --> 01:37:46.470
touianokoro niwa
To that place long ago,

01:37:44.530 --> 01:37:46.920
Hey, where's Ran?!

01:37:46.470 --> 01:37:52.780
amaku soshite setsunai omoi
Gives me an indulging pain.

01:37:47.750 --> 01:37:50.730
Calm down. Calm down and think.

01:37:51.250 --> 01:37:53.430
You found her easily at that time, too.

01:37:52.780 --> 01:37:58.820
komiagetekuru dake
That only leaves me unsettled.

01:37:57.010 --> 01:37:58.190
Come to think of it ...

01:37:58.700 --> 01:38:01.030
How did you know where I was?

01:38:00.180 --> 01:38:05.160
itsudatte bokuno
No matter when,

01:38:01.030 --> 01:38:03.890
You were so caught up in kicking your soccer ball.

01:38:03.890 --> 01:38:07.200
You were kicking the soccer ball the entire time.
Weren't you, Conan-kun?

01:38:05.820 --> 01:38:11.580
muneni arunosa
They will always be in my heart,

01:38:07.200 --> 01:38:08.690
I know it all.

01:38:08.930 --> 01:38:11.750
That's it. That day and today, both times ...

01:38:11.750 --> 01:38:12.570
Uncle!

01:38:12.020 --> 01:38:24.970
yasashisa to iunano omoidetachi
Those memories called kindness.

01:38:12.950 --> 01:38:15.840
Are there any places where you
can hide under the floor?

01:38:17.880 --> 01:38:19.370
I found one!

01:38:24.970 --> 01:38:31.550
omoidetachi ...
Those memories ...

01:38:27.680 --> 01:38:30.360
Damn it. It won't open.

01:38:31.550 --> 01:38:40.240
omoidetachi ...
Those memories ...

01:38:35.910 --> 01:38:36.640
Uncle!

01:38:48.560 --> 01:38:50.070
It broke through!

01:38:50.290 --> 01:38:51.980
Ran! You there, Ran?!

01:38:57.780 --> 01:38:58.990
Dad?

01:38:59.430 --> 01:39:00.540
She's all right.

01:39:00.540 --> 01:39:02.410
We need to hurry, Uncle.

01:39:02.410 --> 01:39:03.920
Damn it!

01:39:07.080 --> 01:39:09.020
This is bad ... This is bad ...

01:39:09.020 --> 01:39:11.880
If we don't turn around the boat soon,
Ran and the others will sink!

01:39:12.330 --> 01:39:14.500
I'm sorry, but I can't do that.

01:39:14.500 --> 01:39:18.390
If we return now, there's a chance that we'll get caught in the whirlpool from the cruiser as it sinks.

01:39:18.390 --> 01:39:19.560
Oh, no!

01:39:24.640 --> 01:39:26.840
It's the rescue chopper from the coast guard!

01:39:26.840 --> 01:39:27.640
Thank goodness!

01:39:34.400 --> 01:39:35.530
It's a rescue chopper!

01:39:38.050 --> 01:39:38.830
This isn't good.

01:39:38.830 --> 01:39:40.080
Let's run to the bow.

01:39:48.080 --> 01:39:49.920
Hey, we're over here!

01:39:50.170 --> 01:39:51.470
Hey!

01:40:05.990 --> 01:40:07.510
Is this everyone?

01:40:07.510 --> 01:40:08.390
Yes.

01:40:08.390 --> 01:40:12.330
Boy, just hold on a little longer.
I'll save you right now.

01:40:12.330 --> 01:40:12.980
OK.

01:40:22.220 --> 01:40:24.470
All right. Hold on tightly, son.

01:40:24.470 --> 01:40:25.040
OK.

01:40:25.390 --> 01:40:29.360
We'll pull you up now.
Support the young lady firmly.

01:40:29.360 --> 01:40:30.420
I got it.

01:40:51.930 --> 01:40:52.850
What happened?

01:41:02.780 --> 01:41:04.160
Grab on!

01:41:07.480 --> 01:41:08.510
Shit!

01:41:25.660 --> 01:41:28.220
Hold on tight, Conan-kun.

01:41:30.040 --> 01:41:31.730
Ran, are you all right?

01:41:40.910 --> 01:41:42.150
Boy!

01:41:43.760 --> 01:41:44.950
Give me your hand.

01:42:17.440 --> 01:42:27.180
hora kyou mo kaze ga hashiru hikari ga nami wo tsukinuke

01:42:17.440 --> 01:42:26.950
Look, the wind runs today too. The light pierces through the waves.

01:42:27.950 --> 01:42:37.960
sono te gutto nobashitara sora ni toduko kigashita

01:42:27.990 --> 01:42:37.630
When I reached out with that hand. I felt that it would reach the sky.

01:42:39.180 --> 01:42:50.000
jibun no shiranai kimi wo mite isshun kowakunaru

01:42:39.180 --> 01:42:49.300
When I see you who doesn't know me. I become frightened for a moment.

01:42:50.000 --> 01:43:00.480
konnanimo kimi ga sukide kotoba ga modokashii

01:42:50.050 --> 01:43:00.150
Even though I love you this much, Your words are impatient.

01:43:00.480 --> 01:43:05.950
natsu wo matsu seiru no you ni kimi no koto wo zutto

01:43:00.480 --> 01:43:05.780
Like the sails that await summer. About you I have always,

01:43:05.860 --> 01:43:11.120
Always, always thought of you.

01:43:05.950 --> 01:43:11.240
zutto zutto omotteiruyo

01:43:11.240 --> 01:43:16.690
taiyou no kanata ippai shippai bakari shita kedo

01:43:11.240 --> 01:43:16.370
With the sun over yonder. I've made nothing but mistakes.

01:43:16.540 --> 01:43:22.300
And disputed together, but now I'm ...

01:43:16.690 --> 01:43:22.510
hanpatsu shiattari demo imawa

01:43:22.880 --> 01:43:32.430
Facing you as one. Because a dream exists there.

01:43:23.050 --> 01:43:33.160
hitotsu ni mukatte iruyo soko ni wa yume ga aru kara

01:43:38.210 --> 01:43:48.190
"gomen ne" no kotoba bakari iu no wa iya dakara

01:43:38.210 --> 01:43:48.110
"I'm sorry" saying nothing but those words, I don't like it, therefore ...

01:43:49.000 --> 01:43:59.200
kimi ni wa "arigatou" no kotoba wo motto motto takusan iitai yo

01:43:49.000 --> 01:43:58.750
To you "thank you" are the words that, I'd like to say much more and more.

01:44:00.060 --> 01:44:10.830
wakari aeteta kimi to mo itsuka ondosa ga atta ne

01:44:00.170 --> 01:44:10.430
You who I knew well ... Sometimes there was a temperature difference.

01:44:10.830 --> 01:44:21.340
soredemo kurushii no wa ittoki dake damon ne

01:44:10.830 --> 01:44:21.150
Even so, it is painful, Only for a short time.

01:44:21.310 --> 01:44:26.440
Like the sails that await summer About you I have always,

01:44:21.340 --> 01:44:26.840
natsu wo matsu seiru no you ni kimi no koto wo zutto

01:44:26.690 --> 01:44:31.910
Always, always wanted to hold you tight.

01:44:26.840 --> 01:44:32.120
zutto zutto dakishimeteitai

01:44:32.070 --> 01:44:37.410
Only to my feelings, I want to stay perfectly honest, but ...

01:44:32.120 --> 01:44:37.580
tada jibun no kimochi ni masshoujiki de itai kedo

01:44:37.580 --> 01:44:43.980
sore de hito wo kizutsukeru koto mo aru ne

01:44:37.700 --> 01:44:43.540
Because of that, people can be wounded.

01:44:43.920 --> 01:44:53.510
I'm facing you as one. Because you are there.

01:44:43.980 --> 01:44:54.820
hitotsu ni mukatte iru yo soko ni wa kimi ga iru kara

01:45:04.430 --> 01:45:09.930
natsu wo matsu seiru no you ni kimi no koto wo zutto

01:45:04.430 --> 01:45:09.610
Like the sails that await summer. About you, I have always,

01:45:09.820 --> 01:45:14.950
Always, always wanted to hold you tight.

01:45:09.930 --> 01:45:15.240
zutto zutto dakishimeteitai

01:45:15.240 --> 01:45:20.620
tada jibun no kimochi ni masshoujiki de itai kedo

01:45:15.240 --> 01:45:20.460
Only to my feelings, Want to stay perfectly honest, but ...

01:45:20.620 --> 01:45:27.060
sore de hito wo kizutsukeru koto mo aru ne

01:45:20.620 --> 01:45:26.630
Because of that people can be wounded.

01:45:27.060 --> 01:45:36.200
hitotsu ni mukatte iru yo soko ni wa kimi ga iru kara

01:45:27.060 --> 01:45:35.970
I'm facing you as one. Because you are there.

01:45:36.140 --> 01:45:42.560
Because you are there.

01:45:36.200 --> 01:45:43.020
soko ni wa kimi ga iru kara

01:46:02.050 --> 01:46:03.190
We're almost there.

01:46:03.190 --> 01:46:04.500
Thank you.

01:46:05.090 --> 01:46:07.170
Your parents' boats are already nearby.

01:46:11.550 --> 01:46:17.680
Then you first figured out that she was the culprit
when you realized Kusaka's alibi plan was too simple?

01:46:17.680 --> 01:46:22.320
Yeah. The reason such a simple alibi plan worked,

01:46:22.320 --> 01:46:27.690
was because the phone partner,
Minako-san, used that alibi as well.

01:46:27.690 --> 01:46:31.960
And the only one who can disguise herself as Chief Takae with her smooth legs,

01:46:31.960 --> 01:46:35.160
is Minako-san, who has the same smooth legs.

01:46:35.160 --> 01:46:40.120
I see. But I'm impressed you
found out where Ran-kun was.

01:46:40.120 --> 01:46:42.000
Oh, that's because ...

01:46:42.000 --> 01:46:44.320
I was more worried than you, you know!

01:46:44.320 --> 01:46:49.670
That time, I was kicking a volley ball,
but Ran-neechan said it was a soccer ball.

01:46:50.280 --> 01:46:54.670
That's why I thought she might be somewhere where she could only hear the sound.

01:46:55.030 --> 01:46:57.060
But it's really disappointing.

01:46:57.060 --> 01:47:03.850
I'm happy that Ran got saved and all, but, I thought the only person that could find Ran was Kudou-kun.

01:47:05.570 --> 01:47:07.280
No. The one who was saved was ...

01:47:07.280 --> 01:47:09.150
Ran-oneesan!

01:47:09.150 --> 01:47:11.650
We fixed the gold medal!

01:47:11.910 --> 01:47:15.650
We've made it so that you can actually put it on your neck with a longer string.

01:47:16.060 --> 01:47:17.530
I'll put it on for you!

01:47:25.590 --> 01:47:26.920
Thank you.

01:47:26.920 --> 01:47:29.050
It looks nice on you.

01:47:29.050 --> 01:47:31.880
I'll treasure it always.

01:47:36.530 --> 01:47:38.300
I was saved ...

01:47:38.900 --> 01:47:43.380
Thanks to those guys' considerate feelings for others.
